WEBVTT

1
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:32.970
Good morning.

2
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.770
Good morning, Capt. Morgan.
What can I do for you today?

3
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:38.230
Same thing as yesterday.

4
00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.440
You and your client wish to make
a temporary exit from the port?

5
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.980
That is right.

6
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.650
- Name?
- Harry Morgan.

7
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.990
- Nationality?
- Eskimo.

8
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.080
- What?
- American.

9
00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.210
- Name of ship?
- <i>Queen Conch</i>, Key West, Florida.

10
00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.460
We're going fishing, like we've done
every day for over two weeks.

11
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.670
We'll be back tonight, and I don't think
we'll go more than 30 miles offshore.

12
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.170
Five francs, please.

13
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.380
One more thing.

14
00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.930
You will go nowhere near the vicinity
of territorial waters...

15
00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.060
Sainte-Lucie, or Dominique.

16
00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.060
- Is that a new order?
- Yes.

17
00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:20.850
The decree was issued last night
by his Excellency, Admiral Robert...

18
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.440
Governor General
of the French West Indies.

19
00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.270
Good for him.

20
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.360
- Why, any complaints?
- No.

21
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.750
Hello, Harry. How's everything?

22
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.670
That feels good.

23
00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.010
- Did you bring me a drink?
- Horatio's bringing it.

24
00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:33.300
You're my pal, Harry.
We sure got them this morning.

25
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.350
- We got them every morning.
- Not last Thursday.

26
00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:39.350
That's right, I forgot. You're right, Eddie.

27
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.810
Here's Horatio. Give him a hand, will you?

28
00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.350
- Good morning, <i>mon Capitaine</i>.
- Good morning.

29
00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.520
- Did you get the bait?
- Yes, sir. Plenty of it.

30
00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:55.320
- That guard took a bottle of our beer.
- Mr. Johnson can afford it.

31
00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.530
- Harry, can I have....
- Just one.

32
00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.040
- Morning.
- Good morning, Mr. Johnson.

33
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.500
- Are we going out?
- That's up to you.

34
00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.420
What sort of a day will it be?

35
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.460
I don't know.
Just about like yesterday. Only better.

36
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.170
- Let's go out, then.
- Okay. Hop aboard.

37
00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.880
- Stand by to cast off.
- All right, <i>mon Capitaine</i>.

38
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.220
- Mr. Johnson.
- Yeah?

39
00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.390
- I got to get some gas.
- All right.

40
00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.270
I'll need money for that.

41
00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.140
How much?

42
00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.940
28 cents a gallon. 40 gallons.

43
00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.190
That'll be $11.20.

44
00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.570
There's $15.

45
00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:35.320
- I'll get you some change at the gas dock.
- Put it against what I owe you.

46
00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.820
Let her go.

47
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.630
Watch it, Johnson.

48
00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.840
There's your strike.

49
00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.800
Put on a little more drag. Not too much.

50
00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.720
You'll have to sock him.
He's gonna jump, anyway.

51
00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.100
Hit him again. Hit him three or four times.
Stick it into him.

52
00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.020
Better get the other teaser in.

53
00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.400
I got him!

54
00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.360
Ease up on that drag.

55
00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.650
He's gone.

56
00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.860
He's not. Ease up on that drag. Quick.

57
00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.040
If he wants to go, let him go.

58
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.590
- He's gone.
- No, he's hooked good.

59
00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.670
- He sure is.
- Reel him in.

60
00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.300
No. I'm sure he's gone.

61
00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.390
I'll tell you when he's gone. Reel in fast.

62
00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.150
- He's gone now.
- Yes, sir, he's gone now.

63
00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:36.400
- He isn't. Turn around and chase him.
- Reel in that line.

64
00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.360
- I can still feel him pull.
- That's the weight of the line.

65
00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.820
You're crazy. I can hardly reel it in.
Maybe he's dead.

66
00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:45.660
Maybe. But he's still jumping out there.

67
00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.760
- Come on. Hurry up.
- I'm hurrying, Mr. Johnson.

68
00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.380
- Can't you put bait on like that, Captain?
- Sure I can.

69
00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:04.760
- Why carry this fellow to do it?
- When the big fish run, you'll see.

70
00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.140
What's the idea?

71
00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.970
He can do it faster than I can.

72
00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.190
A dollar a day
seems like an unnecessary expense to me.

73
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.150
He's necessary. Aren't you, Horatio?

74
00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.560
I hope so.

75
00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.860
Can't Eddie do it?

76
00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.990
No, he can't.

77
00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.320
What's the matter?

78
00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.160
He just lost a fish.

79
00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.160
Mr. Johnson, you're unlucky.

80
00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.080
Would it be all right if I-

81
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.830
- In the icebox. Just take one.
- Thanks.

82
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.920
I don't see why
you want that rummy around.

83
00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:39.170
Eddie was a good man on a boat
before he got to be a rummy.

84
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.420
He's no good now.

85
00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.380
Start her going ahead.

86
00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.800
- Is he related to you or something?
- No.

87
00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.510
- What do you look after him for?
- He thinks he's looking after me.

88
00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.520
All right, let her run.

89
00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.320
- Mr. Johnson.
- Yeah?

90
00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.280
Do you mind if I ask you a question?

91
00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.410
Look, it might interest you to know
I not only bought the beer...

92
00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.830
- but I put a deposit on the bottles.
- Was you ever bit by a dead bee?

93
00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.630
- A dead what?
- A dead honeybee.

94
00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.840
I was never bit by any kind of a bee.

95
00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.920
- You sure?
- Of course I'm sure.

96
00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:24.680
In that case, I'll just finish my nap.
Thanks for the beer.

97
00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.180
Watch that line.

98
00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.690
That's enough for one day.

99
00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:44.700
- What happened?
- Nothing. You just lost a rod and reel.

100
00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:48.240
You had the drag screwed tight.
When the fish struck, you couldn't hold it.

101
00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.660
If you had the harness
buckled down to the reel...

102
00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:53.040
that fish would have taken you
along with him.

103
00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.420
You're just unlucky, Mr. Johnson.
Now, maybe you're lucky with women.

104
00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.340
- What do you say if we go out tonight?
- I'll lucky you, you dirty rummy.

105
00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:03.010
- Are you a good swimmer?
- I've taken all I'm gonna take.

106
00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:05.380
Me, too. Be careful
you don't slip out of my hands.

107
00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.090
Take it easy.
This guy owes you for 16 days.

108
00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:10.680
Fifteen.

109
00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.860
You talk too much, Eddie.

110
00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:22.570
I know it, Harry.

111
00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.070
Okay, forget it.

112
00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.260
What about tomorrow?

113
00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:51.100
I don't think so.
I'm fed up with this kind of fishing.

114
00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.850
I can see how you would be.
Slack that off a little.

115
00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:57.100
You fish for 16 days,
hook a couple of fish any good fisherman...

116
00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.270
would give his life to tie into,
and lose both.

117
00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:02.480
- You're just unlucky. I never seen no one-
- Shut up, Eddie.

118
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.780
You said 16 days. I only owe you for 15.

119
00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:07.530
No. With today it's 16.
Then there's the rod and reel.

120
00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.410
- The tackle's your risk.
- Not when you lose it like you did.

121
00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.660
I paid to rent it every day. It's your risk.

122
00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.620
If you ran a hired car over a cliff,
you'd have to pay for it.

123
00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.120
- Not if he was in it. That's a good one.
- That's good, Eddie.

124
00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.330
You lost the outfit through carelessness.

125
00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.960
It cost me $275.

126
00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.170
I won't charge you for the line, 'cause
a fish so big could've taken it all anyway.

127
00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:31.800
And there's 16 days at $35 a day,
that's $560.

128
00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.970
No, it's $560, Eddie.

129
00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:37.140
You got a little credit,
so that'll be $825 altogether.

130
00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.940
That's what you owe me,
and that's what I want.

131
00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:44.020
I haven't got that much with me.
I'll go to the bank in the morning.

132
00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.650
- That'll be all right?
- I guess it'll have to be.

133
00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.570
- Let's go have a drink.
- Good idea-

134
00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.650
- Stay here and lock up.
- Sure you don't-

135
00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.910
No, Eddie.

136
00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:58.330
Look there. I thought everybody
took their flag in after 6:00.

137
00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.960
- Most of them do.
- That's Vichy for you.

138
00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.710
It's their flag.

139
00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.290
See you later.

140
00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.850
Gentlemen, may I have your names?

141
00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.150
What for?

142
00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:26.270
I heard this gentleman
make a disparaging reference to Vichy.

143
00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.690
I never said anything about Vichy, did I?

144
00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.860
I don't know,
I wasn't paying much attention.

145
00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:33.030
- Your names, please.
- Look, we're Americans....

146
00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:36.660
His name's Johnson. My name's Morgan.
We're living at the Marquis Hotel.

147
00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:38.120
That do you?

148
00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:50.300
Yes, sir?

149
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.130
- What's yours?
- Bourbon.

150
00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.930
Bourbon. And a rum for me.

151
00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:57.010
- Gentlemen, what luck today?
- Not so good, Frenchy.

152
00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:00.930
- We lost the biggest fish I ever saw.
- Maybe tomorrow you hook him again.

153
00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.850
Not me. I'm through. This is my last day.

154
00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.810
- That's too bad.
- Yeah.

155
00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.310
Here's to you.

156
00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.150
I'm gonna clean up.

157
00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.860
- That was $800 and....
- $25.

158
00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.490
$825.

159
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.740
- Johnson.
- Yeah?

160
00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.490
What time tomorrow morning?

161
00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.460
After I get to the bank.
Say around 10:30 or 11:00?

162
00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:25.500
I'll be waiting for you.

163
00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.420
- Any trouble, Harry?
- No, Frenchy.

164
00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:33.420
- Then you are free after today?
- Yeah. Why?

165
00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:37.550
There were some people in here today.
They wanted to hire your boat.

166
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.310
- Fishermen?
- No. Some friends of friends of mine.

167
00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.690
Not a chance.

168
00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.610
- The key, <i>monsieur</i>.
- Thank you.

169
00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.490
Please listen to me, Harry.

170
00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.990
They only want to use your boat
for one night.

171
00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:57.700
- They'll pay you well.
- For what?

172
00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:01.490
I'd like to oblige, but I can't afford
to get mixed up in local politics.

173
00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.080
I would not speak if it weren't important.

174
00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.130
Please, can I go with you to your room?

175
00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.920
Sure. Come ahead.

176
00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.820
Anybody got a match?

177
00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:57.880
Thanks.

178
00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:02.760
Who's that?

179
00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:06.230
She came in this afternoon.
The plane from the south.

180
00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:11.190
Now look, Frenchy, about that other thing.

181
00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.150
I know where you stand
and what your sympathies are.

182
00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.860
It's all right for you,
but I don't want any part of it.

183
00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.820
If I'm caught fooling with you fellas,
my goose'll be cooked.

184
00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.370
Probably lose my boat, too.
I ain't that interested.

185
00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.580
But they are coming to see you tonight.

186
00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.710
You better get word to them.
They'll just be wasting their time.

187
00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.960
Sorry. I'll see you later.

188
00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:47.990
Take over.

189
00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.900
Bravo!

190
00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:37.000
I tried to reach those fellows,
but I can't get in contact with them.

191
00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.880
Who? The ones who wanted
to hire my boat?

192
00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.590
It's dangerous enough for them
to come at all, but to come for nothing-

193
00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.930
I didn't ask to see them.
You better head them off.

194
00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.210
- Hello.
- Let's have it.

195
00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:24.970
- What do you want?
- Johnson's wallet.

196
00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:27.050
- What?
- Come on.

197
00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.430
What are you talking about?

198
00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.890
Mister, what's got into you?

199
00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.940
What do you think you're gonna do?

200
00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:48.700
I'm gonna get that wallet, Slim.

201
00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:51.780
I'd rather you wouldn't call me Slim.

202
00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.370
I'm a little too skinny to take it kindly.

203
00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:56.790
Quit the baby talk.

204
00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.130
Which is it?

205
00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:03.840
You know, Steve,
I wouldn't put it past you.

206
00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:08.380
I didn't know you were a hotel detective.

207
00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:11.600
Johnson's my client.

208
00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.260
He doesn't speak so well of you.

209
00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:15.980
He's still my client.

210
00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:19.810
Pick on somebody to steal from
that doesn't owe me money.

211
00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.270
He dropped it and I picked it up.

212
00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.780
You were gonna give it back to him,
of course?

213
00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.780
No, I wasn't.

214
00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.280
- I don't like him.
- That's a pretty good reason.

215
00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.990
Besides, I need boat fare
to get out of Martinique.

216
00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.160
Another good reason...

217
00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.250
but you'll have to get it
from somebody else.

218
00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.120
- How do you like that?
- Find anything?

219
00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:45.460
About $60 in cash
and about $1,400 in traveler's checks.

220
00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:47.460
Do you expect more?

221
00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:49.840
That bird owed me $825.

222
00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:52.220
"I haven't got that much on me," he says.

223
00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:55.600
"I'll have to go to the bank
and pay you off tomorrow," he says.

224
00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:59.940
And all the time he's got a reservation
on a plane leaving tomorrow at daylight.

225
00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:02.190
So he was gonna skip out on you.

226
00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.860
Your client.

227
00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:07.480
- Good thing you didn't give it back to him.
- Then I did you a favor.

228
00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:09.950
That's right. But if I hadn't stopped you...

229
00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:12.280
you'd have gotten away
with the whole works.

230
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.990
After all, I am entitled to something.

231
00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:17.490
Don't you think so, Slim?

232
00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.540
What do you think is fair?

233
00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.090
I'll leave that to you.

234
00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.170
What would you say to....

235
00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.100
Please, Harry.
I told them, but they insisted-

236
00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:40.100
It is not Gerard's fault, Mr. Morgan.

237
00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.270
Come in and close the door.

238
00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.810
You know,
I told Frenchy I wasn't interested.

239
00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:48.070
I know. But close the door, please.

240
00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.530
I'm very sorry to intrude this way...

241
00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:56.620
- but this is of great importance and we-
- One moment.

242
00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.040
I'd better go.

243
00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:04.790
- See you later.
- Stick around. We're not through yet.

244
00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:07.250
It's all right to talk in front of her, isn't it?

245
00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.050
- Go ahead.
- But it's no good.

246
00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:10.550
- If you'd listen-
- No use.

247
00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:13.340
- You're taking a chance coming here.
- We're not afraid.

248
00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:16.100
I am. I'm sorry, I can't and won't do it.

249
00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.930
We'll give you 2,500 francs.

250
00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:20.720
- That's only $50 in American money.
- It is more to us.

251
00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:24.560
It is only a little voyage
to a place about 40 kilometers from here.

252
00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.400
- We'd give you more money, but we can't.
- It's all we have.

253
00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.940
Don't make me feel bad.
I tell you true, I can't do it.

254
00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:33.400
Afterwards, when things are changed,
it would mean a good deal to you.

255
00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:34.570
Yes, I know.

256
00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:38.200
Mr. Morgan, I thought all Americans
were friendly to our side.

257
00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:41.950
They are. But there's a rumor
that they put fellas on Devil's Island...

258
00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.870
for doing what you're doing.
I'm not that friendly to anybody.

259
00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.080
But they wouldn't do that to an American.

260
00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.090
Do you really think that?

261
00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.090
- Who's that?
- It's me, Harry.

262
00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:54.510
It's all right.

263
00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.760
- Hi, Harry? How you been keeping?
- Hello, Eddie.

264
00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:01.220
- I wanted to talk to you about-
- Could we continue-

265
00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:04.100
Who are you? Who are these guys, Harry?

266
00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.600
Eddie's a friend of mine.

267
00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:07.730
He was hanging around the dock
after you left.

268
00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.820
You have a good memory
for one who drinks.

269
00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.820
Drinking don't bother my memory.
If it did I wouldn't drink.

270
00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:14.650
I couldn't. You see...

271
00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.570
I'd forget how good it was.
Then where would I be?

272
00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:21.410
- I'd start drinking water again.
- Maybe you'd forget about water, too.

273
00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.790
No, I wouldn't. I see too much of it.

274
00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.460
Was you ever bit by a dead bee?

275
00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:33.090
I've no memory of ever being bit
by any kind of bee.

276
00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.220
Were you?

277
00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:38.390
You're all right.
You and Harry's the only ones that-

278
00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:41.260
- Don't forget Frenchy.
- Right. You, Harry and Frenchy.

279
00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:44.390
You got to be careful of dead bees
if you go around barefooted.

280
00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:47.900
If you step on them, they can sting
just as bad as if they was alive.

281
00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:51.190
Especially if they was kind of mad
when they got killed.

282
00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:55.990
- I bet I've been bit 100 times that way.
- You have? Why don't you bite them back?

283
00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:59.530
That's what Harry always says.

284
00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.780
But I ain't got no stinger.

285
00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:05.450
- Does he always talk so much?
- Always.

286
00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:09.330
- What do you want to see me about?
- Oh, yeah, Harry....

287
00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:13.500
I guess I forgot.

288
00:22:13.590 --> 00:22:17.170
That's all right.
I'll see you down at the dock later tonight.

289
00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:19.340
Say, Harry, could you....

290
00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:22.260
Thanks. You're all right. So long.

291
00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:27.730
Sorry. We could stay at this all night
and the answer would still be the same.

292
00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:31.310
I don't care who runs France
or Martinique, or who wants to run it.

293
00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:33.480
You'll have to get somebody else.

294
00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:36.860
Come on, Slim.
We still got some unfinished business.

295
00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:37.950
Good night.

296
00:22:38.030 --> 00:22:41.620
Make yourselves at home, boys.
Cigarettes are on the table over there.

297
00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:49.620
I want to see Johnson's face
when you give it back to him.

298
00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:51.040
All right.

299
00:23:10.770 --> 00:23:13.520
Where've you been?
I've been looking all over for you.

300
00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:15.690
You're a fine one, running off with my girl.

301
00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:18.740
She's got something
she wants to give you. Go ahead, Slim.

302
00:23:18.820 --> 00:23:20.570
Here's your wallet.

303
00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:25.280
- How did you get it?
- I stole it.

304
00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:29.410
That's a fine thing.
What are you gonna do about it?

305
00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:32.750
The question is,
what are you going to do about it?

306
00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:35.460
You'd better look it over
and see if it's all there.

307
00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:37.050
It's all right, I'm sure.

308
00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.380
No, you check it over.
She might want a receipt for it.

309
00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.800
- It's all right. There's nothing missing.
- You sure?

310
00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:46.430
Yeah. Now, young lady, I-

311
00:23:46.510 --> 00:23:49.220
You better count those traveler's checks.

312
00:23:50.390 --> 00:23:53.940
- I know. There's $1,400.
- But you had to go to the bank tomorrow.

313
00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:57.190
What's the time on that plane ticket
you got there?

314
00:23:57.270 --> 00:23:58.360
6:30.

315
00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:01.400
In the morning.
And the bank opens at 10:00.

316
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:12.250
- I don't like him any better than you do.
- I was going to-

317
00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.750
You were going to sign some
of those traveler's checks, weren't you?

318
00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:17.960
- Yeah. Sure.
- Emil, you got a pen handy?

319
00:24:31.890 --> 00:24:34.650
- $825.
- Yeah.

320
00:24:36.690 --> 00:24:38.150
Stay where you are!

321
00:24:49.700 --> 00:24:53.040
- Stay where you are.
- I think I'm sitting on someone's cigarette.

322
00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:24.780
- This is awful.
- Did they get them all?

323
00:25:24.860 --> 00:25:27.950
One got away, at least.
I think it was Beauclere.

324
00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:29.740
Look, Harry, this is bad.

325
00:25:29.830 --> 00:25:32.120
But no one but me knows
that you two saw them.

326
00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:34.120
And Eddie, but he won't remember.

327
00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:38.380
When the police come, you know nothing.
Do you realize, <i>mademoiselle</i>?

328
00:25:38.460 --> 00:25:40.380
Don't be a fool. Stay inside.

329
00:25:56.230 --> 00:25:57.770
<i>Monsieur</i> Gerard!

330
00:26:09.910 --> 00:26:11.700
Cut it out, Cricket.

331
00:26:20.380 --> 00:26:22.750
He couldn't write any faster
than he could duck.

332
00:26:22.840 --> 00:26:25.760
Another minute
and these checks would have been good.

333
00:26:35.930 --> 00:26:39.980
Stay right where you are and keep quiet!
Stay right where you are.

334
00:26:46.940 --> 00:26:49.070
- Who's that?
<i>- Sûreté Nationale.</i>

335
00:26:49.410 --> 00:26:50.860
Gestapo?

336
00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:53.780
Lot of them, isn't there?

337
00:27:09.930 --> 00:27:12.090
- What happened to this man?
- A stray bullet.

338
00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:14.100
His name is Johnson, an American.

339
00:27:14.180 --> 00:27:16.970
- Unfortunate. Take him away.
- Yes, sir.

340
00:27:21.770 --> 00:27:23.150
Call attention.

341
00:27:23.310 --> 00:27:25.320
Your attention, everyone.

342
00:27:26.730 --> 00:27:30.650
All this is regrettable,
but there is no cause for alarm.

343
00:27:31.910 --> 00:27:34.450
We are only interested in those persons...

344
00:27:34.580 --> 00:27:37.620
who have broken the rules
laid down for their behavior.

345
00:27:38.660 --> 00:27:41.330
We shall pick out certain individuals.

346
00:27:42.250 --> 00:27:46.090
Those we do not designate
will leave immediately.

347
00:27:47.340 --> 00:27:51.590
This place will then remain closed
for tonight.

348
00:27:53.680 --> 00:27:54.680
This man.

349
00:27:56.260 --> 00:27:57.260
You.

350
00:28:02.020 --> 00:28:03.690
And <i>mademoiselle</i>.

351
00:28:06.400 --> 00:28:08.690
Was you ever bit by a dead bee?

352
00:28:08.940 --> 00:28:10.740
Come with me, please.

353
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:27.040
I tell you, I didn't know those men.
They came in for a drink. That's all I know.

354
00:28:27.130 --> 00:28:29.590
- You say you never saw these men before?
- No.

355
00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:32.380
What are your sympathies,
<i>Monsieur</i> Gerard?

356
00:28:32.470 --> 00:28:33.550
I am for France.

357
00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:36.180
That is well. Try to remain so.

358
00:28:38.180 --> 00:28:40.600
Let us suggest to <i>Monsieur</i> Gerard...

359
00:28:41.060 --> 00:28:44.440
that the next time suspicious characters
enter his place...

360
00:28:44.850 --> 00:28:46.560
that he notify us.

361
00:28:46.940 --> 00:28:50.690
In that way he may prevent bloodshed
at his doorstep.

362
00:28:50.820 --> 00:28:52.110
I run a public place.

363
00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:54.570
How am I to know who is suspicious
and who is not?

364
00:28:54.660 --> 00:28:57.950
- I think you will know. Good night.
- That is all. You may go.

365
00:28:58.030 --> 00:29:00.410
- Got all of them?
- Beauclere and Emil got away.

366
00:29:00.490 --> 00:29:02.580
- How?
- Jumped off the wagon, ran up an alley.

367
00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:04.830
- Search all the places on your list.
- Yes, sir.

368
00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:08.540
- Continue.
- Did you know these men?

369
00:29:08.710 --> 00:29:09.710
I didn't.

370
00:29:09.840 --> 00:29:12.210
- You did not see them at all in the café?
- Right.

371
00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:14.630
What was your connection
with the dead man?

372
00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:18.140
- He rented my boat to fish from.
- You mean he had rented it.

373
00:29:18.220 --> 00:29:21.810
The tickets in his wallet show
he was to leave Martinique at daylight.

374
00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:24.350
There was no money on him
or in his wallet.

375
00:29:24.640 --> 00:29:27.270
Only some American traveler's checks.

376
00:29:27.730 --> 00:29:29.610
Was that customary with him?

377
00:29:29.730 --> 00:29:31.110
There was $60 in it.

378
00:29:31.190 --> 00:29:32.990
- What happened to it?
- I took it.

379
00:29:33.070 --> 00:29:35.900
- Why?
- Because he owed me $825.

380
00:29:36.070 --> 00:29:39.330
So at least you had no reason to kill him,
did you?

381
00:29:39.910 --> 00:29:43.750
- So it would seem.
- But unfortunately for you, someone did.

382
00:29:43.830 --> 00:29:46.540
As a result of which,
you took it on yourself...

383
00:29:46.960 --> 00:29:48.880
to collect a part of the debt.

384
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.380
- That's right.
- You have this money now?

385
00:29:51.550 --> 00:29:52.800
If you please.

386
00:30:04.640 --> 00:30:06.640
If you please, <i>Capitaine</i>.

387
00:30:06.890 --> 00:30:08.310
This is mine.

388
00:30:08.400 --> 00:30:10.150
How do we know that?

389
00:30:11.820 --> 00:30:14.110
Thank you. Do not be concerned.

390
00:30:14.740 --> 00:30:17.860
This money is impounded
by a government which, like your own...

391
00:30:17.950 --> 00:30:19.740
is at peace with the world.

392
00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:24.330
If your claim is just, it will be discharged.

393
00:30:25.330 --> 00:30:28.170
<i>Mademoiselle.</i> That is all for you.

394
00:30:32.290 --> 00:30:35.460
"Browning, Marie. American, age 22."

395
00:30:35.670 --> 00:30:37.760
How long have you been in Fort de France?

396
00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:39.720
I arrived by plane this afternoon.

397
00:30:39.800 --> 00:30:42.100
- Residence?
- Hotel Marquis.

398
00:30:42.350 --> 00:30:43.850
Where do you come from?

399
00:30:43.930 --> 00:30:45.520
Trinidad. Port of Spain.

400
00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:47.980
And before that,
from where, <i>mademoiselle</i>?

401
00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:51.400
- From home, perhaps?
- No. From Brazil, Rio.

402
00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:53.440
- Alone?
- Yes.

403
00:30:53.820 --> 00:30:56.940
- Why did you get off here?
- To buy a new hat.

404
00:30:57.070 --> 00:30:58.150
Why?

405
00:30:58.280 --> 00:31:00.660
To buy a new... hat.

406
00:31:01.700 --> 00:31:04.240
Read the label.
Maybe you'll believe me then.

407
00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:07.410
I never doubted you, <i>mademoiselle</i>.

408
00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:10.040
It is only your tone that was objectionable.

409
00:31:10.500 --> 00:31:12.210
I'll ask you again.

410
00:31:12.710 --> 00:31:14.710
Why did you get off here?

411
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:17.510
I didn't have money enough
to go any further.

412
00:31:17.590 --> 00:31:20.720
That's better. Where were you
when the shooting occurred?

413
00:31:20.800 --> 00:31:22.590
- I was-
- You don't have to answer.

414
00:31:22.680 --> 00:31:24.390
- Shut up, you.
- Don't answer it.

415
00:31:24.470 --> 00:31:27.220
- I told you to shut up.
- Go ahead. Slap me.

416
00:31:27.310 --> 00:31:29.850
Come, <i>Capitaine</i>. This is not a brawl.

417
00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:31.940
We wish to get to the bottom of this affair.

418
00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:34.150
You'll never do it
by slapping people around.

419
00:31:34.230 --> 00:31:36.070
That's bad luck.

420
00:31:36.150 --> 00:31:37.570
We shall see.

421
00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:42.490
If we need to question you further,
you will be available at the hotel?

422
00:31:42.910 --> 00:31:46.910
I don't know how I'm gonna go any place
when you got my passport and money.

423
00:31:46.990 --> 00:31:49.620
Your passport will be returned to you.

424
00:31:49.790 --> 00:31:51.290
As for the money...

425
00:31:51.370 --> 00:31:55.540
if it is yours,
that will arrange itself in good time.

426
00:31:56.880 --> 00:32:00.920
Do you suggest I see the American Consul
and have him help you arrange it?

427
00:32:01.010 --> 00:32:03.090
That is your privilege.

428
00:32:03.510 --> 00:32:06.850
By the way, what are your sympathies?

429
00:32:07.430 --> 00:32:09.390
- Minding my own business.
- May I-

430
00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:12.480
I don't need any advice
about continuing to do it, either.

431
00:32:12.560 --> 00:32:15.270
- Good night, <i>Capitaine</i>.
- Let's get out of this.

432
00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:28.990
Say, I don't understand all this.
After all, I just got here.

433
00:32:29.200 --> 00:32:31.460
You landed right in the middle
of a small war.

434
00:32:31.540 --> 00:32:32.750
What's it all about?

435
00:32:32.830 --> 00:32:36.340
The boys we just left joined with Vichy.
You know what that is?

436
00:32:36.460 --> 00:32:39.300
- Vaguely.
- They've got the Navy behind them.

437
00:32:39.380 --> 00:32:41.550
- You saw that carrier in the harbor?
- Yeah.

438
00:32:41.630 --> 00:32:45.220
The other fellas they were shooting at,
they're the Free French.

439
00:32:45.300 --> 00:32:48.810
- You know what they are?
- It's not getting any clearer.

440
00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:51.980
Most of the people on the island,
the natives, are patriots.

441
00:32:52.060 --> 00:32:56.230
They're for de Gaulle, but so far they
haven't been able to do much about it.

442
00:32:58.150 --> 00:32:59.900
- Are we in trouble?
- No, Eddie.

443
00:32:59.980 --> 00:33:02.860
- I seen them pick you up and was scared-
- Everything's okay.

444
00:33:02.950 --> 00:33:04.610
Go back and get some sleep.

445
00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:06.820
I'd have got you out. You know me.

446
00:33:06.910 --> 00:33:09.370
I know you, Eddie.
You go on back to the boat.

447
00:33:09.450 --> 00:33:10.950
- Harry, could you-
- No.

448
00:33:11.040 --> 00:33:13.500
- But-
- No more tonight, Eddie. Beat it.

449
00:33:21.010 --> 00:33:24.170
- I could use a drink myself.
- We can get one in here.

450
00:34:01.250 --> 00:34:03.170
What do you wish to drink, sir?

451
00:34:03.260 --> 00:34:04.340
What'll it....

452
00:34:06.220 --> 00:34:08.510
We're just looking around.

453
00:34:09.350 --> 00:34:10.850
Change your mind?

454
00:34:11.010 --> 00:34:13.180
No money. Those guys cleaned me out.

455
00:34:13.270 --> 00:34:14.520
I forgot, too.

456
00:34:15.560 --> 00:34:17.310
Maybe I can do something.

457
00:34:17.810 --> 00:34:20.270
This has been a long day, and I'm thirsty.

458
00:34:22.150 --> 00:34:23.610
Picked him out yet?

459
00:34:24.780 --> 00:34:26.150
You don't mind, do you?

460
00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:30.410
If you're thirsty, go ahead.
If I get tired of waiting I'll be at the hotel.

461
00:34:31.030 --> 00:34:32.030
All right.

462
00:34:44.170 --> 00:34:45.210
May I?

463
00:34:47.760 --> 00:34:48.760
Thanks.

464
00:35:22.210 --> 00:35:23.210
Hello.

465
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:26.090
Come on in.

466
00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:35.010
- You're sore, aren't you?
- Why should I be?

467
00:35:36.470 --> 00:35:39.940
- I didn't behave very well, did I?
- You did all right.

468
00:35:40.730 --> 00:35:42.560
You got the bottle, didn't you?

469
00:35:42.650 --> 00:35:45.650
- You're sore, aren't you?
- Get this straight. I don't give-

470
00:35:45.730 --> 00:35:48.400
I know. You don't give a whoop what I do.

471
00:35:48.490 --> 00:35:52.490
But when I do it you get sore.
After all, you told me to, you know.

472
00:35:52.870 --> 00:35:55.870
- I told you?
- You said go ahead, didn't you?

473
00:35:55.990 --> 00:36:00.410
That's right. I guess I did.
You were pretty good at it, too.

474
00:36:01.330 --> 00:36:02.370
Thanks.

475
00:36:03.040 --> 00:36:05.040
- Would you rather I wouldn't?
- Wouldn't what?

476
00:36:05.130 --> 00:36:06.630
Do things like that.

477
00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:09.510
- Why ask me?
- I'd like to know.

478
00:36:09.880 --> 00:36:13.300
- Of all the screwy-
- All right. I won't do it anymore.

479
00:36:13.390 --> 00:36:15.300
- I didn't ask-
- I know you didn't.

480
00:36:15.390 --> 00:36:18.470
Don't worry.
I'm not giving up anything I care about.

481
00:36:19.980 --> 00:36:22.190
It's like shooting fish in a barrel, anyway.

482
00:36:22.270 --> 00:36:25.190
Men like that. They're all a bunch of....

483
00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:30.650
I'm a fine one to talk.
The pot calling the kettle.

484
00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:34.530
How long have you been away from home?

485
00:36:34.700 --> 00:36:37.620
- This is about the time for it, isn't it?
- Time for what?

486
00:36:37.870 --> 00:36:40.790
The story of my life.
Where do you want me to begin?

487
00:36:40.910 --> 00:36:43.040
I got a pretty fair idea already.

488
00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:45.080
- Who told you?
- You did.

489
00:36:45.380 --> 00:36:48.250
- That slap in the face you took.
- What about it?

490
00:36:48.340 --> 00:36:51.880
You hardly blinked an eye.
It takes a lot of practice to do that.

491
00:36:53.050 --> 00:36:55.300
Yeah, I know a lot about you, Slim.

492
00:36:55.720 --> 00:36:59.010
The next time I get slapped
I better do something about it.

493
00:36:59.220 --> 00:37:01.350
- You forgot your drink.
- I don't want it.

494
00:37:01.430 --> 00:37:03.140
- Who's sore now?
- I am.

495
00:37:23.910 --> 00:37:25.580
- Who is it?
- It's me.

496
00:37:26.540 --> 00:37:28.040
The door's unlocked.

497
00:37:29.090 --> 00:37:32.300
- You forgot your bottle.
- I said I didn't want it.

498
00:37:35.430 --> 00:37:37.140
You are sore, aren't you?

499
00:37:37.890 --> 00:37:39.930
I asked you a question.
You didn't answer me.

500
00:37:40.010 --> 00:37:41.930
I said you're sore, aren't you?

501
00:37:42.020 --> 00:37:44.390
Look, I'm tired
and I want to get some sleep.

502
00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:47.400
That's not a bad idea.
What made you so mad?

503
00:37:48.520 --> 00:37:51.780
- I've been mad ever since I met you.
- Most people are.

504
00:37:52.110 --> 00:37:55.450
One look and you decided
just what you wanted to think about me.

505
00:37:55.530 --> 00:37:57.990
You were.... What's the use?

506
00:37:58.780 --> 00:38:00.490
Go ahead. Keep on going.

507
00:38:01.450 --> 00:38:03.160
You don't know me, Steve.

508
00:38:04.790 --> 00:38:06.170
It doesn't work.

509
00:38:08.210 --> 00:38:11.250
I brought that bottle up here
to make you feel cheap.

510
00:38:11.550 --> 00:38:13.260
That didn't work either.

511
00:38:15.130 --> 00:38:17.430
Instead, I'm the one who feels cheap.

512
00:38:18.260 --> 00:38:20.470
I've never felt that way before.

513
00:38:23.970 --> 00:38:25.140
I wanted....

514
00:38:27.310 --> 00:38:29.310
I thought that maybe....

515
00:38:38.320 --> 00:38:41.870
Go on. Get out of here
before I make a complete fool of myself.

516
00:38:49.420 --> 00:38:51.710
How long have you been away from home?

517
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:54.380
It's none of....

518
00:38:56.840 --> 00:38:58.220
About six months.

519
00:38:58.590 --> 00:38:59.720
Going back?

520
00:39:00.390 --> 00:39:02.810
- How?
- What are you gonna do here?

521
00:39:03.850 --> 00:39:06.230
I don't know. Get a job, maybe.

522
00:39:07.180 --> 00:39:10.560
Jobs are hard to get.
I don't think you'd like it here anyway.

523
00:39:13.190 --> 00:39:15.110
Remind you of somebody, Steve?

524
00:39:18.030 --> 00:39:20.410
This is brand new to me. I like it.

525
00:39:21.240 --> 00:39:23.280
Would you go back if you could?

526
00:39:24.120 --> 00:39:25.240
I'd walk...

527
00:39:27.250 --> 00:39:29.290
if it wasn't for all that water.

528
00:39:46.680 --> 00:39:49.390
Quit worrying, kid.
You'll get back all right.

529
00:40:12.710 --> 00:40:15.340
- What the....
- Here's that bottle again.

530
00:40:18.760 --> 00:40:21.630
It's getting to be quite a problem, isn't it?

531
00:40:23.510 --> 00:40:25.100
- You want a drink?
- No.

532
00:40:26.390 --> 00:40:28.600
I thought you were tired and going to bed.

533
00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:32.270
I know. I thought so, too.
You gave me something to think about.

534
00:40:32.350 --> 00:40:35.440
- You said you might be able to help me.
- That's right.

535
00:40:35.520 --> 00:40:37.520
But how can you do that if....

536
00:40:38.150 --> 00:40:41.820
Are you gonna take that job with those
men that were up here with Frenchy?

537
00:40:41.950 --> 00:40:44.410
Yeah, if I can find what's left of them.

538
00:40:44.490 --> 00:40:48.240
I flew over Devil's Island.
It doesn't look like a high-class resort.

539
00:40:48.580 --> 00:40:51.370
- That's what I heard.
- I don't want to be the cause-

540
00:40:51.460 --> 00:40:55.630
Don't get the idea I'm doing this
just to help you. I need money, too.

541
00:41:00.630 --> 00:41:03.510
Won't Frenchy help you out
without you having to do that?

542
00:41:03.590 --> 00:41:05.180
I don't want his help.

543
00:41:05.470 --> 00:41:07.510
Don't do it, will you, Steve?

544
00:41:08.140 --> 00:41:10.520
- Look, didn't you ask me-
- Don't do it.

545
00:41:12.140 --> 00:41:14.690
Why don't you take this bottle
and go to bed?

546
00:41:17.020 --> 00:41:18.900
Here. Can you use this?

547
00:41:19.150 --> 00:41:21.280
I thought you said you were broke.

548
00:41:22.490 --> 00:41:25.360
You're good. You're awful good.

549
00:41:26.530 --> 00:41:29.330
"I'd walk home
if it wasn't for all that water."

550
00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:36.830
- Who was the girl, Steve?
- Who was what girl?

551
00:41:37.170 --> 00:41:40.050
The one who left you
with such a high opinion of women.

552
00:41:40.130 --> 00:41:42.130
She must have been quite a gal.

553
00:41:43.010 --> 00:41:45.300
You think I lied to you about this,
don't you?

554
00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:47.680
It just happens there's about $30 here.

555
00:41:47.760 --> 00:41:50.470
Not enough for boat fare
or any other kind of fare.

556
00:41:50.560 --> 00:41:53.520
Just enough to be able to say "no"
if I feel like it.

557
00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:55.980
And you can have it if you want it.

558
00:41:57.650 --> 00:41:59.020
I'm sorry, Slim.

559
00:42:01.030 --> 00:42:03.280
But I still say you're awful good
and I wouldn't-

560
00:42:03.360 --> 00:42:06.950
I forgot. You wouldn't take anything
from anybody, would you?

561
00:42:07.030 --> 00:42:08.240
That's right.

562
00:42:09.620 --> 00:42:11.040
You know, Steve...

563
00:42:12.040 --> 00:42:15.710
you're not very hard to figure.
Only at times.

564
00:42:16.960 --> 00:42:19.420
Sometimes I know exactly
what you're going to say.

565
00:42:19.540 --> 00:42:22.840
Most of the time. The other times....

566
00:42:26.550 --> 00:42:28.890
The other times you're just a stinker.

567
00:42:34.810 --> 00:42:38.850
- What did you do that for?
- I've been wondering whether I'd like it.

568
00:42:38.940 --> 00:42:40.400
What's the decision?

569
00:42:41.190 --> 00:42:42.570
I don't know yet.

570
00:42:50.280 --> 00:42:52.280
It's even better when you help.

571
00:42:56.290 --> 00:42:58.670
Sure you won't change your mind
about this?

572
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.590
This belongs to me, and so do my lips.
I don't see any difference.

573
00:43:03.670 --> 00:43:04.710
I do.

574
00:43:05.590 --> 00:43:06.590
Okay.

575
00:43:08.510 --> 00:43:10.800
You know you don't have to act with me.

576
00:43:10.890 --> 00:43:14.060
You don't have to say anything
and you don't have to do anything.

577
00:43:14.140 --> 00:43:15.310
Not a thing.

578
00:43:17.230 --> 00:43:18.980
Maybe just whistle.

579
00:43:23.110 --> 00:43:25.650
You know how to whistle,
don't you, Steve?

580
00:43:25.730 --> 00:43:28.570
You just put your lips together and blow.

581
00:43:50.970 --> 00:43:53.300
Here, chick.

582
00:44:04.820 --> 00:44:06.360
You keep watching.

583
00:44:08.190 --> 00:44:10.200
It's all right. They have gone.

584
00:44:11.410 --> 00:44:12.490
Go on.

585
00:44:13.410 --> 00:44:16.290
You come along the lee shore of Anguilla
from the south.

586
00:44:16.370 --> 00:44:18.120
About three kilometers from the point.

587
00:44:18.200 --> 00:44:21.210
- There's a little cove and a jetty?
- You know it, then.

588
00:44:21.500 --> 00:44:23.710
- The signal's been arranged?
- Emil can show you.

589
00:44:23.790 --> 00:44:25.340
- Emil's not gonna be there.
- Why?

590
00:44:25.420 --> 00:44:27.760
I'm doing this my way. I'm going alone.

591
00:44:29.170 --> 00:44:30.590
What are the signals?

592
00:44:30.670 --> 00:44:33.840
You flash a light to the shore.
They will answer it with two lights.

593
00:44:33.930 --> 00:44:36.850
One held above the other.
There'll be two people to bring back.

594
00:44:36.930 --> 00:44:38.720
- How'll I know them?
- We've never seen them.

595
00:44:38.810 --> 00:44:41.140
We know the name of one only.
Paul de Bursac.

596
00:44:41.230 --> 00:44:44.440
That's good enough.
How about landing them back here?

597
00:44:44.520 --> 00:44:46.400
Do you know Cape Saint-Pierre?

598
00:44:46.480 --> 00:44:50.150
- A boat can meet you offshore there.
- You be on that boat, Frenchy.

599
00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:52.820
I'll get out of here around noon.
Supposedly fishing.

600
00:44:52.910 --> 00:44:56.330
With luck and no patrol boats,
I'll be back in Saint-Pierre at midnight.

601
00:44:56.410 --> 00:44:58.870
I won't be burning any lights,
so keep a sharp lookout.

602
00:44:58.950 --> 00:45:00.540
One thing, Mr. Morgan.

603
00:45:00.910 --> 00:45:04.500
Last night you very definitely refused
to have anything to do with us.

604
00:45:04.580 --> 00:45:06.250
Why have you changed your mind?

605
00:45:06.340 --> 00:45:08.670
I need the money now. Last night I didn't.

606
00:45:08.750 --> 00:45:11.800
- If you knew what this means to us....
- I don't want to know.

607
00:45:11.880 --> 00:45:13.430
I'm glad you're on our side.

608
00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:15.340
I'm not. I'm getting paid.

609
00:45:16.050 --> 00:45:18.810
And by the way, I'd like that money now.

610
00:45:20.020 --> 00:45:23.520
If I were you, I do not think
I would trust Mr. Morgan.

611
00:45:26.860 --> 00:45:28.360
Did a doctor look at his leg?

612
00:45:28.440 --> 00:45:31.400
No. They are watching all doctors
who are friendly to us.

613
00:45:31.490 --> 00:45:34.030
- Miss the bone?
- As far as I can tell.

614
00:45:34.110 --> 00:45:36.070
He's lucky.
Why did you put a pillow under it?

615
00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:38.410
- Why not?
- It doesn't hurt so much that way.

616
00:45:38.490 --> 00:45:40.450
It'll have to hurt, you'll have to take it...

617
00:45:40.540 --> 00:45:43.410
unless you want to take a chance
of gangrene setting in.

618
00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:44.920
All right, I'll take that.

619
00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:46.330
Are you a doctor?

620
00:45:46.710 --> 00:45:49.750
No. But I've handled
quite a lot of gunshot wounds.

621
00:45:50.550 --> 00:45:52.050
You can trust me now.

622
00:45:52.130 --> 00:45:53.470
Good luck, Harry.

623
00:45:56.090 --> 00:45:57.430
It's all right.

624
00:46:08.770 --> 00:46:10.940
- More <i>café, mademoiselle?</i>
- Please.

625
00:46:17.660 --> 00:46:20.330
- What is that you're playing?
- Did you say something?

626
00:46:20.410 --> 00:46:22.040
What's the name of that tune?

627
00:46:22.120 --> 00:46:25.790
It hasn't got any name yet.
I've just been fooling with the lyrics.

628
00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:28.750
They're not so hot, either.
Would you like to hear them?

629
00:46:28.830 --> 00:46:29.840
Sure.

630
00:47:14.130 --> 00:47:15.210
So it goes.

631
00:47:16.300 --> 00:47:18.510
- That's about as far as it goes.
- I like it.

632
00:47:18.590 --> 00:47:20.840
Yes. If I could get the right lyrics.

633
00:47:31.230 --> 00:47:33.860
- Good morning, Cricket.
- Morning, Harry.

634
00:47:33.940 --> 00:47:35.400
- Good morning, Slim.
- Hello.

635
00:47:35.480 --> 00:47:37.950
- How did you sleep?
- The best in a long time.

636
00:47:38.030 --> 00:47:40.660
- Have some coffee?
- No, thanks. I've had mine.

637
00:47:40.860 --> 00:47:43.580
You were up early. What were you doing?

638
00:47:43.660 --> 00:47:47.330
I was getting you a ticket on the plane
this afternoon. It leaves at 4:00.

639
00:47:47.410 --> 00:47:49.370
- Can you make it?
- Sure.

640
00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:53.090
You took that job, didn't you?

641
00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:57.090
See, I figured this way
you wouldn't get your feet wet.

642
00:47:57.170 --> 00:47:58.720
Yeah. That's right.

643
00:47:58.800 --> 00:48:01.260
- That's what you wanted, wasn't it?
- Sure.

644
00:48:01.470 --> 00:48:02.590
I just....

645
00:48:05.640 --> 00:48:09.100
- You want me to go, don't you?
- Yes, I want you to go.

646
00:48:10.190 --> 00:48:11.600
Okay, Steve.

647
00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:14.110
Help her get on that plane,
will you, Cricket?

648
00:48:14.190 --> 00:48:15.650
I sure will, Harry.

649
00:48:15.730 --> 00:48:19.780
I'm gonna be pretty busy from now on,
so I probably won't see you again.

650
00:48:20.280 --> 00:48:22.280
- If I ever get up your way-
- Yeah. Do that.

651
00:48:22.360 --> 00:48:25.780
I'll leave my address with Frenchy
so you can find me.

652
00:48:26.490 --> 00:48:29.120
Maybe I'll know how to whistle by then.

653
00:48:29.580 --> 00:48:31.870
- So long, Slim.
- So long, Steve.

654
00:48:40.050 --> 00:48:42.470
Well, it was nice while it lasted.

655
00:48:43.180 --> 00:48:45.300
Maybe it's better this way, Slim.

656
00:48:45.640 --> 00:48:46.890
I don't know.

657
00:48:47.810 --> 00:48:50.680
You haven't known him very long.
He's a funny guy.

658
00:49:05.450 --> 00:49:09.500
- How are you, Harry? How's everything?
- Fine. I told you to stay at the hotel.

659
00:49:09.580 --> 00:49:12.080
- I knew you was going out.
- Who told you that?

660
00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:14.750
You can't fool me, Harry.
I knew it just as plain.

661
00:49:14.830 --> 00:49:17.590
- Say, could I have a little-
- You're not going.

662
00:49:17.670 --> 00:49:21.130
Could I have a little one,
just enough to fill a hen's ear?

663
00:49:21.510 --> 00:49:23.590
- Come on, Eddie. Get off.
- What's the matter?

664
00:49:23.680 --> 00:49:27.100
There's no sense in getting plugged at me.
Take it easy. You got-

665
00:49:37.860 --> 00:49:39.360
I wouldn't do that to you.

666
00:49:39.440 --> 00:49:42.570
You're right, you wouldn't.
I'm not gonna carry you, that's all.

667
00:49:42.650 --> 00:49:45.740
- What did you have to hit me for?
- So you'd believe me.

668
00:49:45.820 --> 00:49:48.450
- You ain't treating me square.
- Who do you treat square?

669
00:49:48.530 --> 00:49:51.700
You'd double-cross your own mother.
You told me so yourself.

670
00:49:51.790 --> 00:49:53.210
I was only kidding.

671
00:50:02.050 --> 00:50:04.720
Thanks, Harry. I knew you was my pal.

672
00:50:05.510 --> 00:50:08.550
- But why won't you carry me?
- Because I don't want you.

673
00:50:09.220 --> 00:50:11.350
You know, you're just plugged.

674
00:50:11.430 --> 00:50:14.600
Never mind, old pal,
you'll be glad to see me yet.

675
00:50:40.290 --> 00:50:42.210
All right. Come out of there.

676
00:50:44.210 --> 00:50:46.180
It's only me, Harry.

677
00:50:47.340 --> 00:50:49.010
How did you get back on board?

678
00:50:49.090 --> 00:50:51.100
I went up the street for some bottles.

679
00:50:51.180 --> 00:50:53.720
Then I sneaked in
while you was working on the engine.

680
00:50:53.810 --> 00:50:55.850
- I knew you'd carry me.
- Carry you, nothing.

681
00:50:55.930 --> 00:50:58.520
If I thought you could swim back
I'd dump you overboard.

682
00:50:58.600 --> 00:51:01.770
You're a joker. We've got to stick together
when we're in trouble.

683
00:51:01.860 --> 00:51:05.990
- How do you know I'm in trouble?
- You can't fool me. I always know.

684
00:51:06.280 --> 00:51:07.610
Where we going, Harry?

685
00:51:07.700 --> 00:51:09.530
What would you do
if somebody shot at you?

686
00:51:09.620 --> 00:51:11.240
Shot at me? With a gun?

687
00:51:13.540 --> 00:51:16.790
- Who's gonna shoot at me?
- If you're lucky, nobody.

688
00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:20.380
Where we going? What're we gonna do?

689
00:51:20.460 --> 00:51:23.250
I'll tell you when the time comes.
Get out some tackle.

690
00:51:23.340 --> 00:51:25.050
Aren't you glad you came?

691
00:51:26.010 --> 00:51:27.130
No.

692
00:51:39.350 --> 00:51:42.820
- Here. Put this on. It's getting cold.
- I'm all right, Harry.

693
00:51:51.450 --> 00:51:53.700
Say, what's going on?

694
00:51:54.660 --> 00:51:56.750
- What's the matter?
- Nothing.

695
00:51:57.200 --> 00:52:00.370
Yes, there is, too.
What's all the darn guns for?

696
00:52:01.250 --> 00:52:03.340
In case we run into a shark or something.

697
00:52:03.420 --> 00:52:05.000
A shark? At night?

698
00:52:07.010 --> 00:52:10.010
Or something?
What do you mean, "or something"?

699
00:52:10.090 --> 00:52:12.260
- Watch your course.
- What's the matter?

700
00:52:12.340 --> 00:52:15.310
We're going on a job.
I'll tell you what to do when it's time.

701
00:52:15.390 --> 00:52:16.390
A job?

702
00:52:17.430 --> 00:52:20.190
What kind of a job?
What do you expect me to do?

703
00:52:20.350 --> 00:52:21.940
Do you know how to handle this?

704
00:52:22.020 --> 00:52:24.860
Of course I know how.
Everybody knows how to handle a gun.

705
00:52:24.940 --> 00:52:28.440
All you do is work the lever
and pull the trigger. You know I know that.

706
00:52:28.530 --> 00:52:32.450
Such foolish questions.
Do I know how to handle a gun.

707
00:52:37.700 --> 00:52:41.210
- What do I got to work a gun for?
- I just wondered if you could.

708
00:52:41.290 --> 00:52:42.460
You know I can.

709
00:52:42.580 --> 00:52:45.790
Harry, sometimes you act stupid.
Just plain stupid.

710
00:52:46.000 --> 00:52:49.880
Sometimes I think you don't pay
no attention to nothing I say.

711
00:52:54.720 --> 00:52:56.720
Is it gonna be that bad, Harry?

712
00:52:56.810 --> 00:52:59.890
I don't know yet.
It all depends on how lucky we are.

713
00:53:05.610 --> 00:53:07.730
That's why you didn't want to carry me.

714
00:53:07.820 --> 00:53:11.740
I knew there was some other reason.
You wasn't mad at me at all.

715
00:53:16.200 --> 00:53:18.540
You was afraid I'd get hurt.
You was thinking of me.

716
00:53:18.620 --> 00:53:20.330
Watch your course, Eddie.

717
00:53:21.210 --> 00:53:25.080
I feel better now, Harry.
I'll be all right. You'll see.

718
00:53:35.840 --> 00:53:39.100
What's the matter?
What are you looking at me like that for?

719
00:53:40.270 --> 00:53:41.770
What are you laughing at?

720
00:53:41.850 --> 00:53:44.560
Just a joke that neither one of us
knows the answer to.

721
00:53:44.650 --> 00:53:45.690
What joke?

722
00:53:45.770 --> 00:53:47.730
Whether you're gonna hold together
or not.

723
00:53:47.820 --> 00:53:50.820
Don't say that, Harry.
I'm a good man. You know I am.

724
00:53:51.740 --> 00:53:54.950
You are, but you're going
all over the ocean. Stay on your course.

725
00:53:55.240 --> 00:53:56.870
Why do you always....

726
00:54:00.120 --> 00:54:03.120
Could I have just one?
I don't want to get the shakes.

727
00:54:03.620 --> 00:54:06.710
Make it a short one.
I want you rum-brave, not useless.

728
00:54:06.790 --> 00:54:08.130
Thanks, Harry.

729
00:54:28.810 --> 00:54:30.610
What's the matter, Harry?

730
00:54:48.500 --> 00:54:52.340
- Who's that? What are we going to do?
- Pick up a couple of guys.

731
00:54:52.500 --> 00:54:56.180
Here's what I want you to do.
Take this gun and get back in the stern.

732
00:54:56.260 --> 00:54:59.180
If there's any trouble, start shooting.
But don't shoot me.

733
00:54:59.260 --> 00:55:02.010
Supposing something happens to you?
What do I do then?

734
00:55:02.100 --> 00:55:05.230
How do I know?
You invited yourself on this trip, not me.

735
00:55:05.520 --> 00:55:07.270
All right, get back there.

736
00:55:33.880 --> 00:55:36.300
My name's Harry Morgan.
Beauclere sent me.

737
00:55:36.380 --> 00:55:37.800
Get that light out of my face.

738
00:55:38.970 --> 00:55:42.050
- What happened to Beauclere?
- He ran into a little trouble.

739
00:55:42.140 --> 00:55:44.060
- What's your name?
- De Bursac.

740
00:55:44.850 --> 00:55:47.100
That's the name. It's all right, Eddie.

741
00:55:47.730 --> 00:55:49.060
Come on aboard.

742
00:55:49.560 --> 00:55:52.020
Wait a minute.
He didn't say anything about a woman.

743
00:55:52.110 --> 00:55:54.570
Permit me.
This is my wife, <i>Madame</i> de Bursac.

744
00:55:54.650 --> 00:55:56.030
How do you do?

745
00:55:56.110 --> 00:55:58.110
What do you want to bring a....

746
00:56:02.030 --> 00:56:04.910
It's your funeral. Let's get out of here.

747
00:56:23.720 --> 00:56:25.890
All right, Eddie. You can relax now.

748
00:56:27.640 --> 00:56:29.770
Don't unload. We're not home yet.

749
00:56:30.310 --> 00:56:32.980
If she gets cold,
you can put her down in the cabin.

750
00:56:34.440 --> 00:56:36.360
Mr. Morgan, just who are you?

751
00:56:36.900 --> 00:56:40.780
I own this boat. Beauclere's paying me
to get you people back to Martinique.

752
00:56:40.860 --> 00:56:43.410
You're not one of us.
You're not on our side.

753
00:56:43.870 --> 00:56:45.330
I don't understand.

754
00:56:45.410 --> 00:56:48.120
I don't understand
what kind of a war you're fighting...

755
00:56:48.200 --> 00:56:51.500
lugging your wives with you.
Don't you get enough of them at home?

756
00:56:51.580 --> 00:56:53.880
- You say you're being paid for this.
- That's right.

757
00:56:53.960 --> 00:56:56.670
Then I suggest you stop talking
and take us to Martinique.

758
00:56:56.750 --> 00:56:59.010
That's where we're heading right now.

759
00:57:28.200 --> 00:57:30.500
- What's the matter, Harry?
- Keep quiet.

760
00:57:31.830 --> 00:57:34.000
I thought I saw something out there.

761
00:57:36.540 --> 00:57:37.630
Listen.

762
00:57:43.430 --> 00:57:45.180
- What is it?
- I don't know.

763
00:57:45.260 --> 00:57:47.470
Shut up. You hear that?

764
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:50.220
Is it the patrol boat?

765
00:57:50.600 --> 00:57:54.520
Don't you know those engines?
Sounds like she's off there.

766
00:57:58.820 --> 00:58:01.440
Stand by that wheel.
Wait a minute. Give me that gun.

767
00:58:01.530 --> 00:58:03.490
You can't fight them guys, Harry.

768
00:58:03.570 --> 00:58:04.950
What's the matter with you?

769
00:58:05.030 --> 00:58:07.200
You ought to be telling me
how good you are.

770
00:58:07.280 --> 00:58:09.740
I can do it. What do you want me to do?

771
00:58:10.160 --> 00:58:14.250
If we're lucky, nothing. If we're not,
hook her up and get away from here fast.

772
00:58:14.330 --> 00:58:17.380
- What does this mean, Mr. Morgan?
- Trouble, if they see us.

773
00:58:17.460 --> 00:58:19.920
- What can we do?
- You can't do anything.

774
00:58:20.210 --> 00:58:22.880
Just get down on the deck, flat,
and stay there.

775
00:58:23.050 --> 00:58:24.630
But I don't know what good it'll do.

776
00:58:24.720 --> 00:58:27.720
- If you try to resist, we will be killed.
- Shut up, both of you.

777
00:58:27.800 --> 00:58:29.510
Get down on the deck, flat.

778
00:58:29.810 --> 00:58:32.220
You save France. I want to save my boat.

779
00:58:33.430 --> 00:58:35.350
Hook her up, Eddie. Let's go.

780
00:58:38.610 --> 00:58:39.770
Don't shoot!

781
00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:01.750
We got lucky again.

782
00:59:03.800 --> 00:59:07.590
Ease her off and put her on 160
and then get that first-aid kit.

783
00:59:16.140 --> 00:59:17.520
That's not so bad.

784
00:59:17.600 --> 00:59:20.360
You wouldn't have that
if you weren't so anxious to give up.

785
00:59:20.440 --> 00:59:22.070
Please help me get him on the seat.

786
00:59:22.150 --> 00:59:24.690
Leave him. I don't want him
bleeding over my cushion.

787
00:59:24.780 --> 00:59:27.490
- Here you are, Harry.
- You can have a drink now.

788
00:59:27.660 --> 00:59:28.950
Thanks, Harry.

789
00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:32.080
Help me off with his coat.

790
00:59:33.950 --> 00:59:35.200
Easy now, boy.

791
00:59:48.800 --> 00:59:50.390
All right. Get ready.

792
00:59:50.470 --> 00:59:52.890
The man in that boat
will take you on from here.

793
00:59:52.970 --> 00:59:54.810
But I don't understand.

794
00:59:54.890 --> 00:59:57.600
Some people spent a lot of time
figuring this thing out.

795
00:59:57.690 --> 00:59:59.810
They know more about it than we do.

796
01:00:11.450 --> 01:00:12.830
This is de Bursac.

797
01:00:13.200 --> 01:00:16.250
He's the other guy
I was supposed to pick up. His wife.

798
01:00:16.330 --> 01:00:18.290
- My name is Gerard.
- How do you do?

799
01:00:18.370 --> 01:00:21.170
- Easy with him. He's been shot up a little.
- What happened?

800
01:00:21.250 --> 01:00:24.000
We ran into a patrol boat.
They'll tell you about it.

801
01:00:27.090 --> 01:00:29.880
I'll cruise around
and give you a chance to get ashore.

802
01:00:29.970 --> 01:00:31.640
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

803
01:00:50.360 --> 01:00:52.160
Good evening, Mama.

804
01:01:00.210 --> 01:01:03.630
- I thought you said she pulled out.
- I thought she did.

805
01:01:19.480 --> 01:01:20.730
Hello, Steve.

806
01:01:21.230 --> 01:01:22.900
You were going to put her on a plane.

807
01:01:22.980 --> 01:01:26.150
- What's the matter? Didn't it go?
- It went. But I decided not to.

808
01:01:26.230 --> 01:01:29.400
You did? I went to a lot of trouble
to get you out of here.

809
01:01:29.490 --> 01:01:31.360
- That's why I didn't go.
- Yeah.

810
01:01:32.740 --> 01:01:36.030
You dames.
A guy goes out and breaks his neck to....

811
01:01:36.830 --> 01:01:38.830
I might have expected it.

812
01:01:42.210 --> 01:01:43.620
You're not sore, are you?

813
01:01:43.710 --> 01:01:46.920
- It'd be all right-
- I got a refund on that ticket. Here.

814
01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:49.170
That's gonna help a lot.
You better hang onto it.

815
01:01:49.250 --> 01:01:51.010
- We can use-
- She'll buy it for you.

816
01:01:51.090 --> 01:01:53.180
- Nothing but beer for him.
- I'll remember.

817
01:01:53.260 --> 01:01:55.300
We'll be all right. I've got a job.

818
01:01:55.390 --> 01:01:58.760
- Doing what?
- Frenchy seems to think I can sing.

819
01:01:58.970 --> 01:02:00.430
It's his place.

820
01:02:00.600 --> 01:02:03.020
Sometimes you make me so mad I could-

821
01:02:03.100 --> 01:02:04.270
You could do what?

822
01:02:04.400 --> 01:02:05.850
Harry, I need your help.

823
01:02:06.110 --> 01:02:07.440
What is it now?

824
01:02:08.320 --> 01:02:09.730
That's all right. Go ahead.

825
01:02:09.820 --> 01:02:11.780
That man is very badly wounded, Harry.

826
01:02:11.860 --> 01:02:14.910
I looked at him. The bullet hit the gunnel,
it was almost spent.

827
01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:17.660
- All you got to do is take it out.
- Could you do it?

828
01:02:17.780 --> 01:02:21.290
Me? I'm hotter than any doctor.
They would have recognized my boat.

829
01:02:21.370 --> 01:02:22.540
They'll be on my tail soon.

830
01:02:22.620 --> 01:02:25.670
- All I got to do is walk out of here.
- You don't have to go out.

831
01:02:25.750 --> 01:02:28.290
- You didn't bring them here?
- In the cellar.

832
01:02:28.840 --> 01:02:31.880
Why didn't you put them
in a goldfish bowl and be done with it?

833
01:02:31.960 --> 01:02:35.470
We had to do something.
They're watching every road out of town.

834
01:02:35.550 --> 01:02:37.890
See what you got yourself into
by sticking around?

835
01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:39.560
I'm ready to go any time you are.

836
01:02:39.640 --> 01:02:42.770
- Please, Harry, will you do it?
- Not a chance, Frenchy.

837
01:02:43.930 --> 01:02:46.480
Your bill here at the hotel, being overdue...

838
01:02:46.560 --> 01:02:49.650
amounts to 6,356 francs.

839
01:02:50.020 --> 01:02:51.730
She's right, Eddie.

840
01:02:51.820 --> 01:02:53.860
You really keep the books, don't you?

841
01:02:53.940 --> 01:02:57.950
We'll be glad to dismiss the whole matter
if you will do this for us.

842
01:02:59.200 --> 01:03:01.200
- Throw her bill in, too?
- Sure thing.

843
01:03:01.290 --> 01:03:04.290
- All I got to do is take the bullet out-
- That's all.

844
01:03:05.120 --> 01:03:08.500
You almost had me figured right, Mama,
except for one thing.

845
01:03:08.580 --> 01:03:10.000
I'll still owe you that bill.

846
01:03:10.090 --> 01:03:11.800
Up in my room you'll find a medical kit.

847
01:03:11.880 --> 01:03:14.010
It's gray, this big,
has the boat's name on it.

848
01:03:14.090 --> 01:03:16.010
- Bring it to the cellar.
- Sure.

849
01:03:16.130 --> 01:03:18.220
Here's the key. Bring some hot water, too.

850
01:03:18.300 --> 01:03:19.680
This way, Harry.

851
01:03:23.060 --> 01:03:24.100
Can I help?

852
01:03:24.180 --> 01:03:26.980
Just stay out of sight.
If you run across the police...

853
01:03:27.060 --> 01:03:30.440
- don't forget what I told you to tell them.
- What was that, Harry?

854
01:03:31.570 --> 01:03:33.480
Just stay out of sight, Eddie.

855
01:03:34.070 --> 01:03:35.190
I remember.

856
01:04:00.510 --> 01:04:01.850
What do you want here?

857
01:04:01.930 --> 01:04:04.220
I'll tell you. I was sort of invited.
He asked me.

858
01:04:04.310 --> 01:04:05.640
- You're not a doctor.
- No.

859
01:04:05.720 --> 01:04:07.520
- Where's the doctor?
- Please, be patient.

860
01:04:07.600 --> 01:04:09.980
I have been patient.
How do I know you know anything?

861
01:04:10.060 --> 01:04:12.190
- You don't.
- Wait a minute.

862
01:04:28.160 --> 01:04:30.000
How long has he been unconscious?

863
01:04:30.080 --> 01:04:31.540
Just a few minutes.

864
01:04:44.510 --> 01:04:47.060
He's got some fever
and his pulse is a little low.

865
01:04:47.140 --> 01:04:49.230
He'll be all right
when we get the bullet out.

866
01:04:49.310 --> 01:04:52.400
- Don't touch him. Do you hear?
- That's okay. I'm not getting paid.

867
01:04:52.480 --> 01:04:54.860
She doesn't know what she's saying.
She's not herself.

868
01:04:54.980 --> 01:04:57.360
- Who is she?
- Harry, you promised.

869
01:04:58.360 --> 01:05:01.450
You want to help your husband, don't you?
Then use your head.

870
01:05:01.530 --> 01:05:03.870
We can't get a doctor
without giving the show away.

871
01:05:03.950 --> 01:05:06.620
Besides, he's got as good a chance
with me as anybody.

872
01:05:06.700 --> 01:05:08.200
I'm not going to let you do it.

873
01:05:08.290 --> 01:05:10.290
Why not?
He's no different from anybody else.

874
01:05:10.370 --> 01:05:14.040
Just a little sicker, that's all.
It means he's not worth so much.

875
01:05:18.420 --> 01:05:20.300
You can have another crack at me later on.

876
01:05:20.380 --> 01:05:21.800
- Hello, Slim.
- Hello.

877
01:05:21.880 --> 01:05:23.390
Miss Browning, <i>Madame</i> de Bursac.

878
01:05:23.470 --> 01:05:26.100
Don't get tough with Slim.
She's apt to slap you back.

879
01:05:26.180 --> 01:05:28.560
That's what you said you'd do, wasn't it?

880
01:05:28.770 --> 01:05:30.430
Bring the water in here.

881
01:05:30.600 --> 01:05:32.650
- Wait a minute....
- He's trying to help you.

882
01:05:32.730 --> 01:05:35.770
- Who are you?
- Nobody. Just another volunteer.

883
01:05:39.280 --> 01:05:41.900
- Where do you want this water?
- In that basin.

884
01:05:42.860 --> 01:05:44.320
- Is it hot?
- Boiling.

885
01:05:46.700 --> 01:05:50.000
All right, then.
Pour some of this in it. And drop these in.

886
01:05:53.040 --> 01:05:56.340
- Get out of here. You may not like this.
- I'll be all right.

887
01:05:58.090 --> 01:05:59.340
Then take this.

888
01:06:00.260 --> 01:06:01.970
- What is it?
- Chloroform.

889
01:06:02.050 --> 01:06:04.970
Get over by his head.
If he comes to while I'm probing...

890
01:06:05.050 --> 01:06:08.310
pour some of it on a hunk of cotton
and give him a whiff of it.

891
01:06:08.890 --> 01:06:10.980
Don't open it till I tell you to.

892
01:06:12.430 --> 01:06:14.310
Take out about four of those.

893
01:06:18.900 --> 01:06:22.400
George, bring that lamp a little closer
so I can see what I'm doing.

894
01:06:30.740 --> 01:06:31.910
That's good.

895
01:06:35.830 --> 01:06:37.460
All right, Slim.

896
01:06:43.340 --> 01:06:45.090
Hold that a minute.

897
01:06:50.180 --> 01:06:51.470
Easy, boy.

898
01:06:52.310 --> 01:06:54.560
All right, open that can
and give him some.

899
01:06:54.640 --> 01:06:57.310
George, see if you can hold his head down.

900
01:06:57.480 --> 01:06:58.860
Come on, hurry up.

901
01:07:00.980 --> 01:07:04.360
That's fine. Don't worry about her.
Pick up that can.

902
01:07:06.530 --> 01:07:08.870
- Any of it left?
- I think there's enough.

903
01:07:12.870 --> 01:07:16.250
Wait a minute, I don't think we'll need it.
He's out, too.

904
01:07:17.370 --> 01:07:19.590
Bring that lamp down a little lower.

905
01:07:21.050 --> 01:07:23.260
Frenchy, bring that basin over here.

906
01:07:26.800 --> 01:07:30.350
And fan some of those fumes away,
will you, or we'll all be out.

907
01:07:45.150 --> 01:07:48.030
There you are, Frenchy, there's your bullet.

908
01:07:48.780 --> 01:07:51.530
I told you it was spent.
It would have smashed the bone.

909
01:07:51.620 --> 01:07:53.540
All right, I don't need that.

910
01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:12.220
All right, you finish bandaging it up.
Adhesive tape in the box.

911
01:08:12.720 --> 01:08:15.980
I got to get nursie out of here,
or she never will come to.

912
01:08:28.570 --> 01:08:31.070
What are you trying to do,
guess her weight?

913
01:08:31.530 --> 01:08:33.410
She's heftier than you think.

914
01:08:39.420 --> 01:08:42.920
- You'd better loosen her clothes.
- You've been doing all right.

915
01:08:46.590 --> 01:08:49.090
Maybe you'd better
look after her husband.

916
01:08:49.300 --> 01:08:52.010
- He's not gonna run out on me.
- Neither is she.

917
01:08:58.430 --> 01:09:01.600
Is it all right
if I give her a little whiff of this?

918
01:09:18.500 --> 01:09:20.290
You're with us again.

919
01:09:21.210 --> 01:09:23.420
You were lucky. You passed out.

920
01:09:24.920 --> 01:09:26.880
What happened? We must....

921
01:09:26.960 --> 01:09:30.970
We'll talk about that in the morning.
See if you can get some sleep.

922
01:09:32.130 --> 01:09:33.220
Thanks.

923
01:09:50.650 --> 01:09:53.740
Why did you ever come along with him
on a trip like this?

924
01:09:53.820 --> 01:09:57.660
I love him. I want to be with him.

925
01:09:59.200 --> 01:10:02.410
- That's a reason.
- There's another reason.

926
01:10:03.420 --> 01:10:05.880
They told me to come, our people did.

927
01:10:09.380 --> 01:10:13.630
They said no man was much good
if he left someone behind in France...

928
01:10:13.720 --> 01:10:16.100
for the Germans to find and hold.

929
01:10:18.350 --> 01:10:22.020
- That makes sense.
- I told them I'd only be in the way...

930
01:10:22.100 --> 01:10:25.310
that I could do no good, that I was afraid.

931
01:10:27.940 --> 01:10:31.860
But the worst of it is that it's been so hard
for him to have me along...

932
01:10:34.030 --> 01:10:37.950
because I've made him that way, too.
Now he's afraid.

933
01:10:41.080 --> 01:10:42.870
He didn't invent it.

934
01:10:43.540 --> 01:10:45.670
- Invent what?
- Being afraid.

935
01:10:48.840 --> 01:10:50.300
Thanks, Mr. Morgan.

936
01:11:07.730 --> 01:11:09.360
The fever's gone.

937
01:11:11.530 --> 01:11:13.610
Do you....

938
01:11:13.940 --> 01:11:16.570
I'm no doctor,
but he looks pretty good to me.

939
01:11:18.740 --> 01:11:21.620
If he wakes up,
give him another one of these pills.

940
01:11:36.680 --> 01:11:40.350
- Mr. Morgan, I....
- You're not gonna faint again?

941
01:11:41.260 --> 01:11:45.930
No, I'm just having a hard time
trying to say something.

942
01:11:46.060 --> 01:11:48.520
Go ahead, say it. I'm not gonna bite you.

943
01:11:49.730 --> 01:11:52.360
If it hadn't been for you,
Paul might have....

944
01:11:53.780 --> 01:11:55.570
I'm sorry for the way I've acted.

945
01:11:55.650 --> 01:11:59.490
You're not sorry at all, you're just sorry
you made a fool of yourself.

946
01:12:00.410 --> 01:12:01.780
I have, haven't I?

947
01:12:05.660 --> 01:12:08.120
You don't make me angry
when you say that.

948
01:12:08.920 --> 01:12:12.290
I don't think I'll ever be angry again
with anything you say.

949
01:12:13.340 --> 01:12:15.590
Another screwy dame.
Now, how can you....

950
01:12:15.670 --> 01:12:19.640
Good morning. I hate to break this up,
but I've brought some breakfast.

951
01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:23.720
- Good morning.
- How's your patient?

952
01:12:23.810 --> 01:12:26.640
- He'll be all right-
- Or haven't you looked lately?

953
01:12:26.730 --> 01:12:30.150
He'll be all right. I'll be back this evening.

954
01:12:30.730 --> 01:12:33.320
- If you need me before then, call me.
- I will.

955
01:12:33.400 --> 01:12:35.860
Yes, and I hope you have everything
you need here.

956
01:12:35.940 --> 01:12:37.610
The eggs may be a little hardboiled-

957
01:12:37.700 --> 01:12:41.280
- That's all right, I like them that way.
- You're lucky. Isn't she?

958
01:12:47.710 --> 01:12:50.250
I'm gonna get some sleep,
I'll see you later.

959
01:12:54.630 --> 01:12:55.840
Thanks.

960
01:12:57.210 --> 01:12:59.930
- What do you want?
- I could use a match.

961
01:13:08.850 --> 01:13:11.850
Thanks. Now I need a cigarette.

962
01:13:22.950 --> 01:13:26.080
Here, I can do that. Come on, let me help.

963
01:13:26.160 --> 01:13:29.660
When I get ready to take my shoes off,
I'll take them off myself.

964
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:32.170
All right.

965
01:13:33.540 --> 01:13:35.670
- Want something to eat?
- No.

966
01:13:36.670 --> 01:13:40.010
- Just a little breakfast?
- All I want to do is get some sleep.

967
01:13:40.090 --> 01:13:42.890
It's a good idea. I can help you there.

968
01:13:43.840 --> 01:13:47.680
- Now where are you going?
- I'm going to fix you a nice hot bath.

969
01:13:48.140 --> 01:13:49.890
It'll make you sleep better.

970
01:13:49.980 --> 01:13:53.650
I don't want you to take my shoes off,
I don't want you to get me breakfast...

971
01:13:53.770 --> 01:13:55.730
I don't want you to draw me a hot bath...

972
01:13:55.810 --> 01:13:58.900
- I don't want you to-
- Isn't there anything I can do, Steve?

973
01:13:58.980 --> 01:14:01.530
- Yes, get the-
- You know, Mr. Morgan...

974
01:14:01.610 --> 01:14:04.160
you don't make me angry
when you say that.

975
01:14:04.280 --> 01:14:07.950
I don't think I'll ever be angry again
at anything you say.

976
01:14:11.830 --> 01:14:14.540
How am I doing, Steve,
does it work the second time?

977
01:14:14.630 --> 01:14:17.710
You've been wanting
to do something for me, haven't you?

978
01:14:24.050 --> 01:14:25.590
Walk around me.

979
01:14:26.300 --> 01:14:28.760
Go ahead, walk around me, clear around.

980
01:14:40.730 --> 01:14:42.820
- Did you find anything?
- No.

981
01:14:43.820 --> 01:14:48.580
No, Steve.
There are no strings tied to you, not yet.

982
01:15:03.550 --> 01:15:04.800
I like that...

983
01:15:09.220 --> 01:15:10.760
except for the beard.

984
01:15:12.470 --> 01:15:14.310
Why don't you shave...

985
01:15:16.690 --> 01:15:18.230
and we'll try it again.

986
01:15:23.940 --> 01:15:25.780
- Later, Frenchy.
- Harry, wait.

987
01:15:25.860 --> 01:15:28.620
Renard, the Inspector, is downstairs.
You better come down.

988
01:15:28.700 --> 01:15:31.410
- I can't do that, I got to shave.
- He's got Eddie.

989
01:15:32.660 --> 01:15:35.040
He's giving him drinks
and asking him questions.

990
01:15:35.120 --> 01:15:36.830
I was afraid of that.

991
01:15:37.920 --> 01:15:39.840
Good thing you didn't get me in that tub.

992
01:15:39.920 --> 01:15:43.760
Look out for those strings, Steve.
You're liable to trip and break your neck.

993
01:15:43.880 --> 01:15:47.720
- Strings? I didn't see any strings.
- They just don't show, Frenchy.

994
01:15:50.680 --> 01:15:52.180
You ought to have seen that fish.

995
01:15:52.260 --> 01:15:54.430
It must have weighed 900
if it weighed a pound.

996
01:15:54.520 --> 01:15:57.350
It was the biggest marlin you ever seen
in all your born days.

997
01:15:57.440 --> 01:15:59.100
You know, a marlin is a swordfish.

998
01:15:59.190 --> 01:16:02.190
- Good morning, <i>Capitaine</i>.
- Hello, Harry. How's everything?

999
01:16:02.270 --> 01:16:03.860
- Fine.
- Won't you join us?

1000
01:16:03.940 --> 01:16:06.240
It's a little early for this kind of a party.

1001
01:16:06.320 --> 01:16:07.450
Continue, Mr. Eddie.

1002
01:16:07.530 --> 01:16:09.450
Did you hear that? He called me mister.

1003
01:16:09.530 --> 01:16:11.200
Say, you're all right.

1004
01:16:11.660 --> 01:16:14.500
- Was you ever bit by a-
- No, he never was, Eddie.

1005
01:16:14.580 --> 01:16:16.250
Go on with what you were saying.

1006
01:16:16.330 --> 01:16:19.880
I was just telling him about the big one
we hooked onto last night.

1007
01:16:19.960 --> 01:16:23.550
Sir, that fish was so big
that me and Harry could hardly budge him.

1008
01:16:23.630 --> 01:16:26.300
We pumped on him
until we was all wore out, didn't we?

1009
01:16:26.380 --> 01:16:27.880
That's right, Eddie.

1010
01:16:28.180 --> 01:16:30.720
It was after dark
and we was still playing him.

1011
01:16:30.800 --> 01:16:35.020
He must have weighed
at least 1,000 easy.

1012
01:16:36.230 --> 01:16:40.230
Every time Mr. Eddie takes a drink,
this fabulous fish grows larger.

1013
01:16:40.400 --> 01:16:42.980
He must have started
with a pretty small one.

1014
01:16:43.900 --> 01:16:46.320
How did you finally manage
to land such a leviathan?

1015
01:16:46.400 --> 01:16:48.030
We didn't, didn't he tell you?

1016
01:16:48.110 --> 01:16:50.740
- We ran into a German submarine.
- A German submarine?

1017
01:16:50.820 --> 01:16:53.240
Whatever it was,
it turned its light on and fired.

1018
01:16:53.330 --> 01:16:55.290
- I didn't wait to find out.
- I do not think-

1019
01:16:55.370 --> 01:16:57.660
You know,
you can't be too careful these days.

1020
01:16:57.750 --> 01:17:00.750
I do not think anybody
could give a more logical explanation...

1021
01:17:00.830 --> 01:17:04.090
for refusing to obey the challenge
of our patrol boat.

1022
01:17:04.590 --> 01:17:07.090
Not to speak of shooting out
their searchlight.

1023
01:17:07.170 --> 01:17:08.420
- Patrol boat?
- Yes.

1024
01:17:08.510 --> 01:17:10.260
That's what it was. You were right, Eddie.

1025
01:17:10.340 --> 01:17:12.340
I'm a good man in the dark, always was.

1026
01:17:12.430 --> 01:17:15.760
Funny, he kept saying it was a patrol boat,
but I wouldn't believe him.

1027
01:17:15.850 --> 01:17:19.100
There is one thing that is not clear to me,
Capt. Morgan.

1028
01:17:19.480 --> 01:17:20.560
What's that?

1029
01:17:20.640 --> 01:17:24.270
Why does a professional fisherman
go fishing for his own amusement?

1030
01:17:26.320 --> 01:17:29.610
Don't you ever ask any questions?
Don't you ever talk?

1031
01:17:31.070 --> 01:17:33.490
No, I guess you don't.
What were you saying?

1032
01:17:33.570 --> 01:17:37.620
Does a professional fisherman
go fishing for his own amusement?

1033
01:17:38.250 --> 01:17:40.500
He does if he likes it, and we do, don't we?

1034
01:17:40.580 --> 01:17:42.620
Yeah, remember in Key West
when we went-

1035
01:17:42.710 --> 01:17:46.380
- We don't seem to be getting anywhere.
- It was the Fourth of July-

1036
01:17:46.500 --> 01:17:48.840
I was just saying,
Key West, the Fourth of July...

1037
01:17:48.920 --> 01:17:50.800
three years ago at 8:00. I got that in.

1038
01:17:50.880 --> 01:17:53.090
- What about your passengers?
- It was 7:00.

1039
01:17:53.180 --> 01:17:55.550
You oughtn't to burn up at him,
you fed him the rum.

1040
01:17:55.680 --> 01:17:58.310
- What about your two passengers?
- What passengers?

1041
01:17:58.390 --> 01:18:00.230
The ones you brought from Anguilla.

1042
01:18:00.310 --> 01:18:02.560
He was waiting on the dock
when we came in.

1043
01:18:02.650 --> 01:18:04.480
You think I got them ashore in my sleeve?

1044
01:18:04.560 --> 01:18:07.270
You could have landed them anywhere
on our coastline.

1045
01:18:07.360 --> 01:18:08.780
Right, I could've at that.

1046
01:18:08.860 --> 01:18:12.530
- Would $500 refresh your memory?
- My memory's pretty good.

1047
01:18:12.990 --> 01:18:16.160
I remember that you're the guy
who lifted my passport and my money.

1048
01:18:16.240 --> 01:18:20.000
Would your memory become any better if
your passport and money were returned?

1049
01:18:20.080 --> 01:18:22.500
Does that include the $825
Johnson owed me?

1050
01:18:22.620 --> 01:18:25.170
- Why not?
- And the $500 you just mentioned?

1051
01:18:25.710 --> 01:18:28.050
You drive a hard bargain,
<i>Capitaine</i> Morgan.

1052
01:18:28.130 --> 01:18:30.970
That's no bargain.
If these people are so important...

1053
01:18:31.050 --> 01:18:35.010
- they're gonna be pretty hard to find.
- Not for a man of your resourcefulness.

1054
01:18:35.090 --> 01:18:37.510
Think it over and let me hear from you.

1055
01:18:49.570 --> 01:18:51.740
- Did you hear all of that?
- Most of it.

1056
01:18:51.820 --> 01:18:53.570
Bee lips went away pretty mad.

1057
01:18:54.030 --> 01:18:56.410
When he cools off, though,
he's gonna start thinking.

1058
01:18:56.490 --> 01:18:58.870
He thinks now that you will turn them in.

1059
01:18:58.950 --> 01:19:02.290
- Isn't that what you want him to think?
- What will happen then?

1060
01:19:02.370 --> 01:19:04.750
- He hasn't searched this hotel yet, has he?
- Not yet.

1061
01:19:04.830 --> 01:19:05.920
There's your answer.

1062
01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:07.840
He doesn't want them,
but the whole setup.

1063
01:19:07.920 --> 01:19:10.300
- What shall we do?
- It's not we, it's you.

1064
01:19:10.420 --> 01:19:13.630
You can't do anything until that fella
gets strong enough to move.

1065
01:19:13.720 --> 01:19:15.880
Until then, you're probably safe.

1066
01:19:16.050 --> 01:19:17.590
Better get rid of this.

1067
01:19:17.680 --> 01:19:19.510
- Bring us some breakfast.
- Sure.

1068
01:19:19.600 --> 01:19:22.520
- I thought you didn't want any breakfast.
- I didn't then.

1069
01:19:22.600 --> 01:19:25.390
- What were you saying, Eddie?
- I've been figuring.

1070
01:19:25.480 --> 01:19:29.570
Them guys don't think that I'm wise,
but they was trying to get me drunk.

1071
01:19:30.320 --> 01:19:32.480
They don't know me, do they, Harry?

1072
01:19:35.360 --> 01:19:37.410
I think they're trying
to find out something.

1073
01:19:37.490 --> 01:19:38.570
What do you suppose it is?

1074
01:19:38.660 --> 01:19:40.830
- Don't you know?
- I ain't got no idea.

1075
01:19:40.910 --> 01:19:43.500
That's a good way to leave it.
You got the hiccups.

1076
01:19:43.580 --> 01:19:45.960
Have I, Harry? Yeah, I never noticed.

1077
01:19:46.040 --> 01:19:48.830
- You better take a drink of water.
- What, water?

1078
01:19:48.920 --> 01:19:51.750
- That's a good idea, Slim.
- No, not that.

1079
01:19:51.840 --> 01:19:54.130
- It'll do you good.
- I'll be all right.

1080
01:19:55.800 --> 01:19:57.430
- Eddie.
- Yeah, Harry?

1081
01:19:57.510 --> 01:19:59.850
Keep out of sight
and stay away from the police.

1082
01:19:59.930 --> 01:20:02.970
They won't believe
that story you told a second time.

1083
01:20:03.060 --> 01:20:04.810
What story was that, Harry?

1084
01:20:06.350 --> 01:20:07.730
Keep out of sight.

1085
01:22:04.300 --> 01:22:05.680
Seen Eddie around?

1086
01:22:05.760 --> 01:22:08.600
No, sir, Mr. Morgan,
I've not seen him all evening.

1087
01:22:08.930 --> 01:22:10.270
Where's Frenchy?

1088
01:22:48.140 --> 01:22:51.270
I'm going to work. Do you like it?

1089
01:22:51.480 --> 01:22:53.850
You won't have to sing much
in that outfit.

1090
01:22:53.940 --> 01:22:56.650
- You know, sometimes you make me-
- That's why I do it.

1091
01:22:56.730 --> 01:22:59.820
- Haven't seen Eddie, have you?
- No, not since noon, why?

1092
01:22:59.900 --> 01:23:01.900
He left the boat and hasn't come back.

1093
01:23:01.990 --> 01:23:04.320
- Is there anything wrong?
- I don't know.

1094
01:23:04.780 --> 01:23:07.450
Don't look now,
but over there at the second table...

1095
01:23:07.530 --> 01:23:10.540
there's a guy with a mustache.
I think he's following me.

1096
01:23:10.620 --> 01:23:13.500
Keep an eye on him, will you?
I'm going downstairs.

1097
01:23:14.160 --> 01:23:16.420
Stick around awhile, she's going to sing.

1098
01:23:16.500 --> 01:23:18.630
- I'll be right back.
- Give her my love.

1099
01:23:18.710 --> 01:23:21.050
I'd give her my own if she had that on.

1100
01:23:21.510 --> 01:23:24.170
Here's the rest of the lyrics, Slim.
How do you feel?

1101
01:23:24.260 --> 01:23:27.140
- I could use a drink, Cricket.
- Sure, come on.

1102
01:23:29.100 --> 01:23:31.810
- What will you have, Slim?
- Scotch and soda.

1103
01:23:32.270 --> 01:23:33.350
Same.

1104
01:23:44.320 --> 01:23:46.530
- Good evening.
- Good evening, Capt. Morgan.

1105
01:23:46.610 --> 01:23:49.410
- How are you feeling?
- Much better. I'm very grateful to you.

1106
01:23:49.490 --> 01:23:51.990
Forget it. Let me have a look at this.

1107
01:23:54.910 --> 01:23:56.620
- There's no bleeding.
- No.

1108
01:23:58.210 --> 01:24:00.040
- Does that hurt?
- Very little.

1109
01:24:00.130 --> 01:24:03.420
My only trouble is when I'm eating.
I'm awkward with my left hand.

1110
01:24:03.510 --> 01:24:07.340
We'll see if we can have you shot
in the other arm next time.

1111
01:24:07.470 --> 01:24:09.300
You won't need me anymore.

1112
01:24:10.760 --> 01:24:12.100
Frenchy, I'm pulling out.

1113
01:24:12.180 --> 01:24:13.600
- When?
- Soon as I find Eddie.

1114
01:24:13.680 --> 01:24:15.230
- Is your friend missing?
- Yeah.

1115
01:24:15.310 --> 01:24:16.350
What happened?

1116
01:24:16.440 --> 01:24:18.730
I don't know,
he left the dock and hasn't been back.

1117
01:24:18.810 --> 01:24:21.730
- Usually does what I tell him.
- I'm sorry if anything happened.

1118
01:24:21.820 --> 01:24:24.820
- I won't know until I find him.
- Couldn't you leave him here?

1119
01:24:24.900 --> 01:24:26.740
I don't think Eddie would like that.

1120
01:24:26.820 --> 01:24:28.450
Frenchy, as soon as I'm gone...

1121
01:24:28.530 --> 01:24:30.950
Renard will move in
and turn this place upside down...

1122
01:24:31.030 --> 01:24:34.290
so you better start figuring
how and where you're gonna move him.

1123
01:24:34.370 --> 01:24:37.920
- Wouldn't it be best if we went with you?
- Why do you want to go?

1124
01:24:38.000 --> 01:24:41.840
I'm still trying to get out of the jam
I got into bringing you here.

1125
01:24:41.920 --> 01:24:43.670
Why'd you come here in the first place?

1126
01:24:43.750 --> 01:24:46.670
I know why she came, she told me,
but why did you?

1127
01:24:46.760 --> 01:24:48.630
Have you heard of Pierre Villemars?

1128
01:24:48.720 --> 01:24:52.640
Pierre Villemars? Yeah, I read a headline.
He was quite a guy.

1129
01:24:52.930 --> 01:24:55.180
- Vichy got him. He's dead, isn't he?
- No.

1130
01:24:55.270 --> 01:24:58.060
He's on Devil's Island.
They sent me here to get him...

1131
01:24:58.140 --> 01:25:00.060
to bring him back here to Martinique.

1132
01:25:00.150 --> 01:25:03.070
He's a man whom people
who are persecuted and oppressed...

1133
01:25:03.150 --> 01:25:04.940
will believe in and follow.

1134
01:25:07.400 --> 01:25:09.820
Just how are you gonna get him away?

1135
01:25:10.780 --> 01:25:13.240
You don't think much of me,
Capt. Morgan.

1136
01:25:13.330 --> 01:25:16.790
You're wondering why they've chosen me
for this mission.

1137
01:25:16.870 --> 01:25:18.250
I wonder, too.

1138
01:25:18.660 --> 01:25:21.330
As you know, I'm not a brave man.

1139
01:25:23.170 --> 01:25:25.630
On the contrary, I'm always frightened.

1140
01:25:27.010 --> 01:25:29.840
I wish I could borrow your nature
for a while, Captain.

1141
01:25:29.930 --> 01:25:32.260
When you meet danger,
you never think of anything...

1142
01:25:32.340 --> 01:25:34.470
except how you will circumvent it.

1143
01:25:34.680 --> 01:25:38.310
The word failure
does not even exist for you, while I....

1144
01:25:40.560 --> 01:25:43.610
I think always, "Suppose I fail"...

1145
01:25:44.770 --> 01:25:46.530
and then I am frightened.

1146
01:25:46.780 --> 01:25:49.860
Yeah, I can easily see how
it wouldn't take much courage...

1147
01:25:49.950 --> 01:25:52.320
to get a notorious patriot
off Devil's Island.

1148
01:25:52.410 --> 01:25:56.950
But just for professional reasons,
I'd like to know how you're gonna do it.

1149
01:25:57.040 --> 01:25:58.660
We will find a way.

1150
01:25:59.000 --> 01:26:01.870
It might fail, and if it does...

1151
01:26:02.080 --> 01:26:05.340
and I am still alive...

1152
01:26:06.460 --> 01:26:10.050
I will try to pass on my information,
my mission, to someone else.

1153
01:26:10.590 --> 01:26:13.140
Perhaps to a better man,
who does not fail.

1154
01:26:13.430 --> 01:26:15.800
Because there is always someone else.

1155
01:26:17.640 --> 01:26:19.930
That is the mistake
the Germans always make...

1156
01:26:20.020 --> 01:26:22.060
with people they try to destroy.

1157
01:26:23.150 --> 01:26:26.020
There will be always someone else.

1158
01:26:28.940 --> 01:26:31.570
Originally, we planned
to do everything from here.

1159
01:26:31.650 --> 01:26:35.030
But then, because of my own clumsiness,
it was impossible.

1160
01:26:35.660 --> 01:26:38.240
And that's the reason
we have to go with you.

1161
01:26:38.580 --> 01:26:41.580
I couldn't get you on the dock,
there's a man there watching...

1162
01:26:41.660 --> 01:26:43.830
there's one upstairs, they're everywhere.

1163
01:26:43.920 --> 01:26:47.040
- How would I get you through the streets?
- How will you go?

1164
01:26:47.130 --> 01:26:48.800
They're watching me to find you.

1165
01:26:48.880 --> 01:26:52.170
As long as I haven't got you along,
I can at least get on the boat.

1166
01:26:52.260 --> 01:26:55.090
There'll be a fog,
and the tide will turn after midnight.

1167
01:26:55.180 --> 01:26:57.550
I can cut loose,
drift out beyond the breakwater...

1168
01:26:57.640 --> 01:26:59.350
before I start my engines.

1169
01:27:00.140 --> 01:27:02.430
I'll still have trouble enough,
even without you.

1170
01:27:02.520 --> 01:27:04.770
- But, Harry-
- Capt. Morgan is right.

1171
01:27:06.520 --> 01:27:08.400
This is not his fight yet.

1172
01:27:09.150 --> 01:27:13.650
Some day I hope it may be,
because we could use him.

1173
01:27:15.200 --> 01:27:17.120
You have done enough for us already.

1174
01:27:17.200 --> 01:27:20.950
Gerard told me of your refusing
Renard's offer to give us up.

1175
01:27:21.950 --> 01:27:24.120
How do you know I won't do it yet?

1176
01:27:24.580 --> 01:27:27.040
There are many things a man will do...

1177
01:27:27.380 --> 01:27:31.880
but betrayal for a price is not one of yours.

1178
01:27:34.800 --> 01:27:36.140
Good luck.

1179
01:27:37.220 --> 01:27:39.470
- I hope you find your friend.
- Thanks.

1180
01:27:39.560 --> 01:27:41.270
Goodbye, and thanks.

1181
01:27:46.400 --> 01:27:49.440
Frenchy, I got a few things
to talk to you about before I blow.

1182
01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:51.980
Then I'll be up in a little while, Harry.

1183
01:27:56.410 --> 01:27:57.820
Any sign of Eddie?

1184
01:27:58.700 --> 01:28:01.790
- Your friend's still sitting at his table.
- I know.

1185
01:28:01.870 --> 01:28:04.540
- What's the matter, Steve?
- I don't know.

1186
01:28:04.620 --> 01:28:07.170
I think the whole thing's gonna blow up,
it's too quiet.

1187
01:28:07.250 --> 01:28:09.460
- What will you do?
- We'll leave tonight...

1188
01:28:09.540 --> 01:28:11.170
as soon as I find Eddie.

1189
01:28:11.250 --> 01:28:14.510
We're leaving here for good,
the three of us.

1190
01:28:15.420 --> 01:28:17.720
Wait, I want you to know
what you're getting into.

1191
01:28:17.800 --> 01:28:19.890
It'll be rough, I'm broke. If we get out...

1192
01:28:19.970 --> 01:28:22.600
it'll be with a few hundred gallons of gas
and a few francs.

1193
01:28:22.680 --> 01:28:25.020
Just enough to get us
to Port-au-Prince maybe.

1194
01:28:25.100 --> 01:28:26.690
I've never been there.

1195
01:28:27.190 --> 01:28:30.690
I don't know when you'll get back home.
It could be a long time.

1196
01:28:31.020 --> 01:28:33.730
It could be forever,
or are you afraid of that?

1197
01:28:34.490 --> 01:28:38.070
I'm hard to get, Steve.
All you have to do is ask me.

1198
01:28:39.370 --> 01:28:41.580
How long will it take you to pack?

1199
01:28:42.700 --> 01:28:45.660
There's a lot of people around here,
save it.

1200
01:28:48.710 --> 01:28:51.920
We won't shove off till midnight.
Go ahead and go to work.

1201
01:28:56.800 --> 01:28:59.930
- All set, Slim?
- Sure, but don't make it sad, Cricket.

1202
01:29:00.010 --> 01:29:03.260
- I don't feel that way.
- You don't look that way, either. Let's go.

1203
01:29:03.350 --> 01:29:04.890
Top note, boys.

1204
01:30:48.040 --> 01:30:49.870
<i>Madame</i> de Bursac wants to see you.

1205
01:30:49.950 --> 01:30:52.710
- Look, Frenchy, that's all over.
- She's up in your room.

1206
01:30:52.790 --> 01:30:54.000
Why did you....

1207
01:30:54.080 --> 01:30:56.460
Please, Harry, that's all I will ask.

1208
01:30:57.710 --> 01:30:59.170
Thanks, Harry.

1209
01:31:03.800 --> 01:31:05.970
You shouldn't have come, it's too risky.

1210
01:31:06.050 --> 01:31:07.220
I told you I can't take you.

1211
01:31:07.300 --> 01:31:11.060
I didn't come up for that.
You've already done too much for us...

1212
01:31:11.140 --> 01:31:13.690
but there's just one other favor
I'd like to ask.

1213
01:31:13.810 --> 01:31:15.650
I want you to take these.

1214
01:31:15.730 --> 01:31:18.400
They were my grandmother's,
and her mother's before that.

1215
01:31:18.480 --> 01:31:22.240
She gave them to me when I got married.
They're all I've got left.

1216
01:31:22.320 --> 01:31:25.700
I want you to take them out of here
and save them till we can-

1217
01:31:25.780 --> 01:31:27.700
Suppose they get me before I get out?

1218
01:31:27.780 --> 01:31:30.910
Then throw them overboard,
at least they won't have them.

1219
01:31:31.200 --> 01:31:33.250
Suppose you never come for them?

1220
01:31:33.330 --> 01:31:36.250
Then let it be a part payment
for all you've done for us.

1221
01:31:36.330 --> 01:31:37.710
Please, won't you?

1222
01:31:38.340 --> 01:31:41.050
Steve, Renard just came in,
he's on his way up.

1223
01:31:41.130 --> 01:31:43.260
- Did he see you?
- I don't think so.

1224
01:31:45.090 --> 01:31:48.890
All right, you take these,
both of you get in there and keep quiet.

1225
01:31:48.970 --> 01:31:51.520
As soon as I get rid of him,
take her back to the cellar.

1226
01:31:51.600 --> 01:31:52.680
All right.

1227
01:32:03.110 --> 01:32:04.950
Good evening, may we come in?

1228
01:32:09.950 --> 01:32:11.330
Good evening.

1229
01:32:12.120 --> 01:32:13.790
No, I never carry them.

1230
01:32:15.660 --> 01:32:16.750
What's on your mind?

1231
01:32:16.830 --> 01:32:19.380
The whereabouts of the two people
we are searching for.

1232
01:32:19.460 --> 01:32:21.130
- You haven't found them yet?
- No.

1233
01:32:21.210 --> 01:32:24.880
But since morning, through our sources,
we've learned their names...

1234
01:32:24.970 --> 01:32:28.590
<i>Monsieur</i> and <i>Madame</i> de Bursac.
That is correct, is it not?

1235
01:32:28.680 --> 01:32:31.680
- How would I know that?
- I thought perhaps....

1236
01:32:34.350 --> 01:32:35.770
Very nice perfume.

1237
01:32:37.440 --> 01:32:39.480
- You like that?
- Yes.

1238
01:32:40.770 --> 01:32:43.480
So do I. All right, Slim, come out.

1239
01:32:47.530 --> 01:32:50.280
- You've met the boys.
- Good evening.

1240
01:32:50.490 --> 01:32:54.240
<i>Mademoiselle.</i> Now we are all here.

1241
01:32:54.790 --> 01:32:59.000
Except your friend, Mr. Eddie,
as he likes to be called.

1242
01:33:03.710 --> 01:33:05.340
- So you got him.
- Yes.

1243
01:33:05.550 --> 01:33:07.680
Now we lack only
the two missing persons.

1244
01:33:07.760 --> 01:33:09.010
What're you gonna do with him?

1245
01:33:09.090 --> 01:33:12.640
If you will not give us
the information we want, perhaps he will.

1246
01:33:13.180 --> 01:33:15.640
Before we made the mistake
of giving him liquor...

1247
01:33:15.770 --> 01:33:17.350
this time we will withhold it.

1248
01:33:17.430 --> 01:33:19.440
- You know what that'll do to him?
- I think so.

1249
01:33:19.520 --> 01:33:22.940
- He couldn't stand it, he'd crack up.
- You could easily prevent that.

1250
01:33:23.020 --> 01:33:24.400
Yeah, I can.

1251
01:33:26.070 --> 01:33:27.570
You got a cigarette?

1252
01:33:29.360 --> 01:33:32.870
- Can't you make him talk?
- When necessary.

1253
01:33:35.290 --> 01:33:37.580
You'll find some in that drawer, Slim.

1254
01:33:38.960 --> 01:33:43.130
You could save Mr. Eddie a great deal of,
shall we say, discomfort?

1255
01:33:45.880 --> 01:33:49.430
And me a lot of time,
if you will tell us where these people are.

1256
01:33:56.770 --> 01:33:58.640
How much were you going to give me?

1257
01:33:58.730 --> 01:34:00.350
More than what's mine already?

1258
01:34:00.440 --> 01:34:04.020
I do not think now
I will have to pay anybody anything.

1259
01:34:07.570 --> 01:34:09.150
You're probably right.

1260
01:34:11.410 --> 01:34:13.700
- I haven't got a match.
- Don't go any....

1261
01:34:15.370 --> 01:34:17.790
All right, go on, get them up. Go on.

1262
01:34:18.660 --> 01:34:20.960
Pull your guns, go ahead.

1263
01:34:21.040 --> 01:34:23.790
Get them out. Go ahead and try it!

1264
01:34:26.380 --> 01:34:28.460
- You're gonna get it, anyway.
- Don't.

1265
01:34:28.550 --> 01:34:30.510
You've been pushing me around
long enough.

1266
01:34:30.590 --> 01:34:34.180
You were gonna drive Eddie nuts.
Picking on a poor old rummy that never....

1267
01:34:34.260 --> 01:34:36.970
Slapping girls around.
That's right, go for it!

1268
01:34:37.850 --> 01:34:39.770
Your boy needs company.

1269
01:34:47.400 --> 01:34:50.940
Look at that, ain't that silly?

1270
01:34:53.950 --> 01:34:55.990
That's how close you came.

1271
01:34:57.490 --> 01:34:59.660
All right, Frenchy, get their guns.

1272
01:35:11.090 --> 01:35:12.550
Here you are.

1273
01:35:18.310 --> 01:35:21.230
Now get over on that couch.
Go ahead, step over him.

1274
01:35:25.020 --> 01:35:26.270
Sit down.

1275
01:35:29.980 --> 01:35:31.860
All right, come on out.

1276
01:35:34.860 --> 01:35:37.200
That's one of them,
the other one's in the cellar.

1277
01:35:37.280 --> 01:35:38.870
Take her down, get some help.

1278
01:35:38.950 --> 01:35:41.620
Have them ready to leave on the boat,
then come back here.

1279
01:35:41.700 --> 01:35:44.040
Slim, you pack.
We'll leave as soon as we get Eddie.

1280
01:35:44.120 --> 01:35:45.120
Okay, Steve.

1281
01:35:45.250 --> 01:35:47.250
- Just how do you think you-
- Shut up.

1282
01:35:47.330 --> 01:35:50.210
You want to know
how I'm gonna get him out?

1283
01:35:50.880 --> 01:35:53.220
That broke as easy as you will.

1284
01:35:53.300 --> 01:35:54.720
There's a phone in the hall.

1285
01:35:54.800 --> 01:35:57.390
You're gonna tell someone to let him go,
send him here.

1286
01:35:57.470 --> 01:35:59.470
Yes, you are, one of you.

1287
01:36:01.850 --> 01:36:03.810
I haven't forgotten you.

1288
01:36:05.770 --> 01:36:08.310
You'll both take a beating
till someone uses that phone.

1289
01:36:08.440 --> 01:36:10.730
So one of you
is gonna take a beating for nothing.

1290
01:36:10.820 --> 01:36:14.650
I don't care which one it is.
I'll start with you.

1291
01:36:16.780 --> 01:36:19.240
You will release him immediately.

1292
01:36:21.080 --> 01:36:24.750
- Tell him you'll explain later.
- I will explain it later.

1293
01:36:25.160 --> 01:36:28.920
Tell him to send him back to the hotel
and do nothing else till you get there.

1294
01:36:29.000 --> 01:36:33.260
Send him back here to the hotel
and do nothing until you hear from us.

1295
01:36:37.010 --> 01:36:40.390
All right, inside.
You've got some harbor passes to fill out.

1296
01:36:43.600 --> 01:36:46.060
And now Paul and <i>Madame</i> de Bursac.

1297
01:36:49.480 --> 01:36:51.520
I'll be right with you, Frenchy.

1298
01:37:01.620 --> 01:37:04.120
- They're all yours now.
- Thanks, Mr. Morgan.

1299
01:37:05.370 --> 01:37:06.620
They are all ready.

1300
01:37:06.710 --> 01:37:08.870
These will get them past the guard
and on the boat.

1301
01:37:08.960 --> 01:37:10.540
Where will you take them?

1302
01:37:10.630 --> 01:37:12.290
- Maybe Devil's Island.
- What?

1303
01:37:12.380 --> 01:37:15.050
Might even get Villemars off,
wasn't that what you wanted?

1304
01:37:15.130 --> 01:37:18.300
Very much. Why are you doing this, Harry?

1305
01:37:19.970 --> 01:37:21.430
I don't know.

1306
01:37:21.930 --> 01:37:25.100
Maybe because I like you,
maybe because I don't like them.

1307
01:37:25.180 --> 01:37:27.640
I'm glad you are on our side, Harry.

1308
01:37:27.730 --> 01:37:29.480
No kissing, Frenchy.

1309
01:37:30.310 --> 01:37:33.980
- You'll have to take care of those guys.
- We will give you plenty of time.

1310
01:37:34.070 --> 01:37:36.820
If you let them go,
they'll come back and burn this place.

1311
01:37:36.900 --> 01:37:39.030
Let them, it will be a very small fire.

1312
01:37:39.110 --> 01:37:43.280
When Villemars comes back,
it'll be our turn. We'll start a bigger one.

1313
01:37:43.370 --> 01:37:44.870
Meet you on the boat.

1314
01:37:46.000 --> 01:37:47.620
One minute, please.

1315
01:37:47.710 --> 01:37:49.830
That's all right, let him through.

1316
01:37:53.170 --> 01:37:56.090
- How are you, Harry? How's everything?
- It's all right now.

1317
01:37:56.170 --> 01:37:58.840
You look glad to see me.
You know a funny thing-

1318
01:37:59.340 --> 01:38:01.890
Don't know what they wanted,
but they wouldn't give me-

1319
01:38:01.970 --> 01:38:05.100
I'll get you one down on the boat.
We're leaving, Eddie.

1320
01:38:05.180 --> 01:38:06.970
- Ready, Slim?
- In a minute, Steve.

1321
01:38:07.060 --> 01:38:08.520
Close that, will you?

1322
01:38:08.600 --> 01:38:12.020
- Say, what is this, is she going with us?
- Yeah, it looks like it.

1323
01:38:12.100 --> 01:38:14.270
Harry, you mean.... What's she got....

1324
01:38:14.860 --> 01:38:18.150
- Who are you?
- Was you ever bit by a dead bee?

1325
01:38:19.450 --> 01:38:20.700
- Was you?
- Yeah.

1326
01:38:20.780 --> 01:38:22.660
You got to be careful of dead bees.

1327
01:38:22.740 --> 01:38:24.740
They can sting you just as bad
as live ones.

1328
01:38:24.830 --> 01:38:27.580
Especially if they was kind of mad
when they got killed.

1329
01:38:27.660 --> 01:38:29.540
I feel like I was talking to myself.

1330
01:38:29.620 --> 01:38:32.170
I bet I've been bit 100 times that way.

1331
01:38:33.130 --> 01:38:37.050
- Why don't you bite them back?
- I would. Only I haven't got a stinger.

1332
01:38:39.010 --> 01:38:42.590
I remember you. You're all right.
She can come, it's okay with me.

1333
01:38:42.680 --> 01:38:44.390
I'll have both of you to take care of.

1334
01:38:44.470 --> 01:38:47.560
That's right, Eddie.
You can begin by grabbing these bags.

1335
01:38:47.640 --> 01:38:49.100
Come on, Slim.

1336
01:39:08.040 --> 01:39:10.370
Do I have time to say goodbye to Cricket?

1337
01:39:10.450 --> 01:39:11.870
Sure, go ahead.

1338
01:39:20.090 --> 01:39:21.670
- I came to say goodbye.
- What?

1339
01:39:21.760 --> 01:39:24.470
We're leaving now. Thanks for everything.

1340
01:39:24.550 --> 01:39:27.930
- Hey, Slim. Are you still happy?
- What do you think?
